2
00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:47.780
<i> [man]
 There's a legend of a man
 who lives beneath the sea.</i>

3
00:00:47.813 --> 00:00:49.849
<i> He is a fisher of men.</i>

4
00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:53.786
<i> The last hope of all those
 who have been left behind.</i>

5
00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:57.390
<i> Many survivors claim to have
 felt his gripping hands
 beneath them.</i>

6
00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.258
<i>pushing them up to the surface.</i>

7
00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:02.195
<i> whispering strength
 until help could arrive.</i>

8
00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:06.299
<i> But this. of course.
 is only a legend.</i>

9
00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:11.137
[man] Help!

10
00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.440
- [woman yelling]
- [man] Over here!

11
00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:20.713
- [both gasping]
- [man] Help!

12
00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:25.151
Ma'am. I'm a Coast Guard rescue
swimmer. I'm here to help you.

13
00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:26.886
- Sir.
- Here.

14
00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:30.123
Stay with your flotation.
I'll be back for you.

15
00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.425
- Don't leave me!
- Stay there.

16
00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.527
[man] Don't you leave me!

17
00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:37.330
[whimpering]

18
00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:40.733
Basket is outside
the cabin door. going down.

19
00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:43.269
-<i> [pilot] Roger. Copy you.</i>
- Boarder. right 30.

20
00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:44.570
Boarder. right 15.

21
00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:47.340
-<i> [pilot] Right 15.</i>
- Hold. hold. hold.

22
00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.542
Basket is in the water.

23
00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:52.211
Swimmer and survivor
have the basket.

24
00:01:52.244 --> 00:01:54.180
Put your head in for me.

25
00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:56.549
- [gasping]
- Help me.

26
00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.518
[coughing] Take it up!

27
00:01:58.817 --> 00:02:00.353
[man] Easy forward.

28
00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.787
Let go!

29
00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.923
- No.
- Let go!

30
00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:07.226
- Let go. you're drowning her!
- [grunting]

31
00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:09.262
Help me.
Help me. please. [grunts]

32
00:02:09.294 --> 00:02:10.162
[woman whimpering]

33
00:02:11.062 --> 00:02:12.499
Whoa! Swimmer just popped him
in the face.

34
00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:19.205
OK. he's putting the man
in the basket.

35
00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:21.207
Man is in the basket.

36
00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.877
Taking the load.

37
00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:28.581
[screaming]

38
00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:30.517
Whoa. Big wave.

39
00:02:35.287 --> 00:02:38.558
Get out! Get out! What's wrong
with you? Sit there and shut up.

40
00:02:58.477 --> 00:03:01.414
[man] Swimmer in sight.

41
00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.252
Prepare to take the load.

42
00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:09.422
I have the
ready-for-pickup signal.

43
00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:18.664
Swimmer is approaching
cabin door.

44
00:03:18.697 --> 00:03:23.269
Survivor looks unconscious.

45
00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:25.871
Swimmer inside of cabin door.

46
00:03:25.904 --> 00:03:30.276
- [coughing. gagging]
- Cabin door closed.

47
00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:34.614
- [continues coughing]
- [radio chatter]

48
00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.689
[man retching]

49
00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:45.858
God. I think you just
broke my nose.

50
00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:48.461
And you may have killed
your wife. sir!

51
00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:51.964
Twenty minutes
to Kodiak.

52
00:03:51.997 --> 00:03:54.667
[man] Roger.
He's giving her CPR.

53
00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:57.270
[pilot] Com-tech Kodiak.
this is Coast Guard 6096.

54
00:03:57.303 --> 00:04:00.273
We have two hypothermic
survivors on board.

55
00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:03.543
Be there in 20 minutes.
Requesting an ambulance
on scene when we land.

56
00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.463
[gasping. crying]

57
00:04:24.496 --> 00:04:26.699
[man chuckling] Whoa!
There we go.

58
00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:28.901
- [man] Got her?
- We got her!

59
00:04:37.776 --> 00:04:40.346
[laughing]

60
00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:42.581
[radio chatter]

61
00:04:42.614 --> 00:04:46.452
[continues laughing]
That a way. baby!

62
00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:50.423
- [woman coughing]
- There's dead...

63
00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.491
[exhales]

64
00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:54.694
...and then there's dead.

65
00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:58.031
[man] I swear
you get better with age.

66
00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:02.535
[exhales]

67
00:05:14.646 --> 00:05:19.952
[indistinct chatter]

68
00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:25.057
[woman] Oh. we're not
going home.

69
00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.760
- Had to hit him. huh?
- Yeah.

70
00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:29.695
You are not...
Stay over there!

71
00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:32.531
You stay over there
until you hear me!
Don't come near me.

72
00:05:32.564 --> 00:05:36.336
Seems like it's always
the big ones that crack.

73
00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:38.638
Lieutenant.

74
00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:42.108
Crew said that she went under.
They thought you'd lost her.

75
00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:44.977
Lucky guess.

76
00:05:46.044 --> 00:05:48.414
Luck my ass.

77
00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:52.585
[indistinct radio chatter]

78
00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:11.537
I didn't think you were serious.

79
00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.473
Of course you didn't. Ben.
How could you think I was
serious?

80
00:06:14.506 --> 00:06:16.442
I'm not some nameless
drowning victim.

81
00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:20.480
Oh. gee. I'm sorry saving lives
doesn't jibe with our social
cal...

82
00:06:21.713 --> 00:06:26.485
[stammering] That's. um...
That's my chair.

83
00:06:26.518 --> 00:06:29.455
He's right.
Not that chair.

84
00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:34.126
I'm sorry. I was just pointing
things out in the living room.
They didn't know.

85
00:06:34.159 --> 00:06:37.163
I would never take your chair.

86
00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:46.672
Pick it up. What's...?

87
00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:50.743
It doesn't have
to be messy. Ben.

88
00:06:50.776 --> 00:06:54.514
It's clean. simple for both
of us. We don't have kids.

89
00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:58.818
Well. what about Friday?

90
00:07:01.653 --> 00:07:03.155
What about Friday?

91
00:07:03.188 --> 00:07:07.159
We were gonna go with Carl
and Bridgette. you know.
to that...

92
00:07:07.192 --> 00:07:09.094
...dinner dance thing
at the base.

93
00:07:09.127 --> 00:07:13.199
[exhales] The base?
All you can eat wings?

94
00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:16.735
A dart game to settle the tab?
That's the date we can't break?

95
00:07:16.768 --> 00:07:18.904
- You're right. You're right.
- Wow.

96
00:07:18.937 --> 00:07:23.876
Look. we'll... We'll go away.
all right? Just us.

97
00:07:23.909 --> 00:07:25.110
It's too late. Ben.

98
00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:28.514
I don't know what I can say to
you that I haven't said already.

99
00:07:28.547 --> 00:07:30.683
It's time for me
to rescue myself.

100
00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:32.785
[phone ringing]

101
00:07:37.956 --> 00:07:40.526
Maybe. uh... Maybe I should
be the one to move out.

102
00:07:40.559 --> 00:07:42.661
<i> - [machine]
 You've reached Helen...
 - [Ben] And Ben.</i>

103
00:07:42.694 --> 00:07:44.464
<i> Leave a message.</i>

104
00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:47.900
I don't even know where
anything is in this house.
It's much easier this way.

105
00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:51.170
<i> [man over machine]
 Senior Chief.
 please report to base. [beeps]</i>

106
00:07:51.203 --> 00:07:55.674
I can... I can fix this.
All right? I...

107
00:07:55.707 --> 00:07:57.510
I can...

108
00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:01.113
I can fix this. Just...

109
00:08:02.247 --> 00:08:06.585
Tell me what to do.
Tell me what to do.

110
00:08:06.618 --> 00:08:08.855
- [beeping]
- [sighs]

111
00:08:10.722 --> 00:08:12.691
[beeping continues]

112
00:08:12.724 --> 00:08:13.826
Just let me go.

113
00:08:13.859 --> 00:08:17.897
- No. No.
- Just let me go.

114
00:08:23.602 --> 00:08:25.671
[beeping]

115
00:08:25.704 --> 00:08:30.142
You should answer that.

116
00:08:30.175 --> 00:08:34.280
<i>[man on radio]
Ready rescue helo 6096.
Swimmer one. return to base.</i>

117
00:08:34.313 --> 00:08:37.917
- I don't want to lose her.
- Then change.

118
00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.619
Man. how many times we had
this conversation. huh?

119
00:08:40.652 --> 00:08:42.187
The only way
for you to save it

120
00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:45.791
is to give this up
and fly a desk.

121
00:08:45.824 --> 00:08:48.928
Exactly.
She just wants to live.

122
00:08:50.295 --> 00:08:53.666
Hey. maybe we can get a hobby.
Both of us.

123
00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:56.735
- Something like fishing.
- Fishing?

124
00:08:56.768 --> 00:08:59.738
- Yeah.
- Guys like us don't fish. Carl.

125
00:08:59.771 --> 00:09:02.942
It'll work out.
Always does.

126
00:09:03.208 --> 00:09:04.743
Let me ask you something.
seriously.

127
00:09:04.776 --> 00:09:06.946
Is it too soon
for me to ask her out?

128
00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:09.181
- You better...
- I guess so.

129
00:09:09.214 --> 00:09:11.817
[waves crashing]

130
00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:13.919
<i> [man on radio]
 Mayday. mayday. mayday.</i>

131
00:09:13.952 --> 00:09:16.822
<i>This is cargo vessel</i> Sea Queen.

132
00:09:16.855 --> 00:09:19.758
<i> We're at 55 degrees.
 12 minutes North.</i>

133
00:09:19.791 --> 00:09:22.328
<i> 167 degrees. 10 minutes West.</i>

134
00:09:23.996 --> 00:09:26.999
<i> We're taking on water.
 We're abandoning ship.</i>

135
00:09:27.299 --> 00:09:29.735
I repeat. we're abandoning ship.

136
00:09:29.768 --> 00:09:31.303
You make sure you
and the four men...

137
00:09:31.336 --> 00:09:34.674
[speaking foreign language]

138
00:09:36.341 --> 00:09:37.843
Son. look at me.
Look at me.

139
00:09:37.876 --> 00:09:40.779
You're gonna be OK. Got that?

140
00:09:40.812 --> 00:09:43.782
We're gonna be OK. OK.

141
00:09:43.815 --> 00:09:45.918
[beeping. electric whirring]

142
00:09:45.951 --> 00:09:49.922
[howling. gusting winds]

143
00:09:49.955 --> 00:09:52.625
[helicopter blades whirring]

144
00:09:56.695 --> 00:09:58.897
[beeping]

145
00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:02.067
- We have a tail rotor de-ice
caution light.
- Any secondary?

146
00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.837
No. Circuit breakers are in
so it definitely has failed.

147
00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.271
We're not building up any ice.

148
00:10:06.304 --> 00:10:08.941
- How's the fuel?
- 40 minutes to bingo.

149
00:10:08.974 --> 00:10:10.743
All right. take the stick.

150
00:10:10.776 --> 00:10:13.245
- OK. I have the controls.
- All right. huddle time. boys.

151
00:10:13.278 --> 00:10:15.748
We have a de-ice fail.
We're low on fuel.

152
00:10:15.781 --> 00:10:17.750
The rulebook says
we cut our losses.

153
00:10:17.783 --> 00:10:19.652
What do you think. Ben?

154
00:10:19.685 --> 00:10:23.956
Well. if we go home...
they die. Bill.

155
00:10:26.358 --> 00:10:30.329
<i> [pilot] Kodiak.
 this is Coast Guard 6096.</i>

156
00:10:30.362 --> 00:10:31.730
<i> We have a tail rotor de-ice
 caution light.</i>

157
00:10:31.763 --> 00:10:33.432
but we are pressing on.

158
00:10:33.465 --> 00:10:35.768
<i> [man] 609er 6. keep us updated
 on your status.</i>

159
00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:38.070
-<i> [pilot] 6096 status...</i>
- Get the maintenance chief.

160
00:10:38.103 --> 00:10:40.873
I wanna know
what he thinks about this.

161
00:10:43.475 --> 00:10:46.745
[waves crashing]

162
00:10:46.778 --> 00:10:49.982
[man grunting. yelling]

163
00:10:58.323 --> 00:11:00.726
<i> [man 1] Computer is saying
 winds at 60-85 knots.</i>

164
00:11:00.759 --> 00:11:03.362
<i> You're on your own
 with altitude.</i>

165
00:11:03.395 --> 00:11:04.296
<i> [man 2] Roger.</i>

166
00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:07.032
Mark. Mark. Right side.
Debris in water.

167
00:11:07.065 --> 00:11:09.702
- Request to open cabin door.
-<i> [man 1] Roger. Open door.</i>

168
00:11:11.002 --> 00:11:14.106
<i> [man 2] Kodiak Ops.
 6096. we're on scene.</i>

169
00:11:14.139 --> 00:11:17.043
<i>We have heavy debris in the
water. Commencing cover search.</i>

170
00:11:31.923 --> 00:11:34.993
Mark in known position.

171
00:11:35.026 --> 00:11:37.029
I'm going in.

172
00:11:39.397 --> 00:11:42.901
They're dead. Ben.
Ben. they're dead.

173
00:11:42.934 --> 00:11:44.136
We don't know that.

174
00:11:45.237 --> 00:11:47.906
There's six PIW's all tied
together. No signs of life.

175
00:11:47.939 --> 00:11:51.176
- I think we may be too late.
- Not our call.

176
00:11:51.209 --> 00:11:53.445
They're on scene.
They'll make the assessment.

177
00:11:53.478 --> 00:11:55.781
Requesting to get wet. sir.

178
00:11:55.814 --> 00:11:58.050
I ain't sending you fishing
for bodies. Not in this.

179
00:11:58.083 --> 00:12:00.019
Well. how about
fathers and sons?

180
00:12:03.088 --> 00:12:05.991
Flare! Flare!
We got a live one here.
we got a live one.

181
00:12:08.794 --> 00:12:12.498
You got five minutes.
Then we're hauling
your ass back up.

182
00:12:12.531 --> 00:12:14.800
<i> [man] Kodiak Ops.
 this is Coast Guard 6096.</i>

183
00:12:14.833 --> 00:12:17.202
<i> We have people in the water
 and we are deploying
 our swimmer.</i>

184
00:12:17.235 --> 00:12:19.772
[man] 609er 6. Kodiak Ops. copy.

185
00:12:19.805 --> 00:12:22.074
[Carl] One's holding the flare.
I see no other movement.

186
00:12:22.107 --> 00:12:24.376
- [pilot] Roger that.
- [Carl] Swimmer's ready.

187
00:12:24.409 --> 00:12:27.113
- Check swimmer.
- Roger. Checking swimmer.

188
00:12:30.916 --> 00:12:33.552
Swimmer's dress-down
checklist is complete.

189
00:12:33.585 --> 00:12:35.521
Five minutes.

190
00:12:39.124 --> 00:12:40.793
[Carl] Swimmer's away.

191
00:12:48.433 --> 00:12:52.505
- Swimmer's OK. Clear back
and left 40.
- Clear back and left.

192
00:13:12.257 --> 00:13:16.896
- How we looking on fuel. there?
- Two minutes to bingo.

193
00:13:23.268 --> 00:13:26.271
I'm a Coast Guard rescue swimmer
here to help you. son.

194
00:13:26.304 --> 00:13:29.575
You're gonna be OK. I'm gonna
get you in that helicopter.

195
00:13:34.913 --> 00:13:38.050
- I have the
ready-for-pickup signal.
- Roger.

196
00:13:42.921 --> 00:13:45.858
Basket is going out
of the cabin door.

197
00:13:46.658 --> 00:13:48.594
Bingo. We're at bingo. Gotta go.

198
00:13:48.627 --> 00:13:51.997
[Carl] Ease it back. Hold.
The basket is in the water.

199
00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:54.032
We're out of time.
We gotta go. Carl.

200
00:13:54.065 --> 00:13:56.568
[Carl] Hold position.
Steady. Hold.

201
00:13:56.601 --> 00:13:59.137
He's putting the survivor
in the basket.

202
00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:03.209
-<i> [man] ...going crazy.</i>
- Yeah. I know.
I'm all over the place.

203
00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.215
Come on. Carl.
We gotta go. now!

204
00:14:10.248 --> 00:14:12.852
[Carl] Don't have a
ready-for-pickup signal yet.

205
00:14:14.619 --> 00:14:19.525
- Carl! Carl! Behind you!
- Holy shit!

206
00:14:20.992 --> 00:14:22.228
We lost our tail rotor.

207
00:14:24.663 --> 00:14:27.299
- [grunting]
- Mayday. Mayday. Mayday.

208
00:14:29.301 --> 00:14:31.570
[screaming]

209
00:14:31.603 --> 00:14:35.007
- We're going down.
- Mayday. Mayday.

210
00:15:12.577 --> 00:15:15.581
[gasping]

211
00:15:20.118 --> 00:15:22.387
- Carl.
- I'm here.

212
00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:25.257
- Carl.
- Ben.

213
00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:27.659
Hold on. Carl.

214
00:15:27.692 --> 00:15:29.361
Hold on.

215
00:15:29.394 --> 00:15:32.131
They'll be coming for us.

216
00:15:34.632 --> 00:15:37.669
I've got you.
You're OK now.

217
00:15:37.702 --> 00:15:41.273
- You're OK. I'm here. Carl.
- [gasping. coughing]

218
00:15:41.306 --> 00:15:45.210
We're OK. Hang on.
I've got you.

219
00:15:45.243 --> 00:15:48.080
[Carl] You think
they're coming?

220
00:15:48.113 --> 00:15:50.182
[Ben] Oh. yeah.
They're coming.

221
00:15:52.117 --> 00:15:54.186
I want a C-130
over that crash site now.

222
00:15:54.219 --> 00:15:57.389
- Lieutenant Krauss.
start the mishap checklist.
- Aye. captain.

223
00:15:57.422 --> 00:15:59.358
I've got an EPIRB hit
on Randall's survivor suit.

224
00:15:59.624 --> 00:16:01.159
Launch ready helo.
swimmer provide.

225
00:16:01.192 --> 00:16:03.295
We have a C-130 coming off
from KCAW at two.

226
00:16:03.328 --> 00:16:06.031
- It's already low on fuel.
- I don't care. Cut an engine.

227
00:16:06.064 --> 00:16:08.033
I want him to know
he's not alone out there.

228
00:16:13.271 --> 00:16:15.007
Listen.

229
00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:16.375
[airplane engine whirring]

230
00:16:16.674 --> 00:16:18.744
You hear that?

231
00:16:32.724 --> 00:16:37.396
Hold on. Carl.
Here we go. I've got you.

232
00:16:39.297 --> 00:16:41.099
What's the ETA
on the backup helo?

233
00:16:41.132 --> 00:16:44.136
En route to Cold Bay.
Should be on scene three.
maybe four hours.

234
00:16:44.169 --> 00:16:45.104
Make it three.

235
00:16:54.446 --> 00:16:58.150
- [sighs]
- [vomiting. coughing]

236
00:16:58.183 --> 00:17:02.320
Jesus. how much more of that
stuff do you think I got in me?

237
00:17:02.353 --> 00:17:05.223
- You feel that?
- [gasping]

238
00:17:05.256 --> 00:17:07.426
- You feel that?
- [groaning] Yeah.

239
00:17:07.459 --> 00:17:12.097
It means you're alive.
I'm not gonna let go.

240
00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:15.100
- Don't you!
- I'm not gonna.

241
00:17:15.133 --> 00:17:18.237
I'm not gonna.

242
00:17:27.512 --> 00:17:31.717
[shivering. groaning]

243
00:17:53.204 --> 00:17:56.775
[helicopter blades whirring]

244
00:18:10.221 --> 00:18:12.791
Serious fractures like in the
C-spinal should cause paralysis.

245
00:18:12.824 --> 00:18:16.561
Mostly what we see is old
fractures in the arms.
also in the leg.

246
00:18:16.594 --> 00:18:18.330
But nothing acute. nothing new.

247
00:18:21.566 --> 00:18:26.171
[indistinct chatter]

248
00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:09.447
We've been friends a long time.
haven't we? I've always been
good to you. haven't I?

249
00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:13.251
Didn't promote you to a desk
when you turned 40
like everybody else.

250
00:19:13.284 --> 00:19:16.621
- That's right.
- All right. so now I need you
to listen to me.

251
00:19:16.654 --> 00:19:18.824
OK.

252
00:19:20.258 --> 00:19:22.527
There's an instructor opening
at "A" School in...

253
00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:26.264
- No. The answer is no.
- You just said you'd listen.

254
00:19:26.297 --> 00:19:29.367
- Sit down.
- I'm not interested. captain.

255
00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:32.237
Well. it's no longer a request.
Senior Chief. Sit down.

256
00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:34.273
You're serious?

257
00:19:42.013 --> 00:19:44.382
You have two choices.

258
00:19:44.415 --> 00:19:46.918
Sign the papers today and you
can live life as a civilian

259
00:19:46.951 --> 00:19:49.621
here in Kodiak
if that's what you want.

260
00:19:49.887 --> 00:19:52.390
Or you can take that "A" School
opening I'm offering you.

261
00:19:52.423 --> 00:19:55.360
- [scoffs]
- I've already spoken
to command down there.

262
00:19:55.393 --> 00:19:57.662
It will be your class.
You will be in charge.

263
00:19:57.695 --> 00:20:01.433
You can take the time to work
your way back into shape.

264
00:20:01.466 --> 00:20:02.934
- I am in shape.
- Goddamn it.

265
00:20:02.967 --> 00:20:05.204
That's not
what I'm talking about.

266
00:20:06.304 --> 00:20:07.606
[exhales]

267
00:20:07.639 --> 00:20:10.875
Ben. all I'm asking is that you
go down there for a few months.

268
00:20:10.908 --> 00:20:13.578
You work with the kids.
you recharge. you...

269
00:20:13.611 --> 00:20:17.349
...download that epic résumé
where it's gonna do some good.

270
00:20:19.384 --> 00:20:22.320
You can't always be the one
in the water. Ben.

271
00:20:22.353 --> 00:20:25.324
You'll know when you're
ready to come back.

272
00:20:51.349 --> 00:20:53.919
- [marching cadence]
- [whistle blowing]

273
00:21:11.736 --> 00:21:15.473
You people got 15 seconds
to get off this bus!

274
00:21:15.506 --> 00:21:18.343
- [man 1]Move! Move. let's go!
- [man 2]Get off the bus!

275
00:21:18.376 --> 00:21:20.912
[indistinct yelling]

276
00:21:32.457 --> 00:21:33.959
[electronic whirring]

277
00:21:37.562 --> 00:21:39.998
[man] Put your white books
in your red bags.

278
00:21:40.031 --> 00:21:42.767
Let's get that squared away now.
Put those books away.

279
00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:45.403
Put down your bags.
Fall out to the rear.

280
00:21:45.436 --> 00:21:47.539
Follow two flights
and patter up the hall.

281
00:21:47.572 --> 00:21:50.408
The rest of you. pick a bunk.
Put on your ODU's.

282
00:21:50.441 --> 00:21:53.545
You started with 15 minutes.
You are now down to 12. Move!

283
00:21:53.578 --> 00:21:55.347
Move. move. move. move!

284
00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:57.615
- Short time. short time.
- One. two...

285
00:21:57.648 --> 00:21:59.718
- Over here.
- [man] Hurry up. move it out.

286
00:21:59.751 --> 00:22:01.419
- Top.
- All right.

287
00:22:01.452 --> 00:22:03.655
[man] Find your rack.
Quit wasting my time.

288
00:22:03.688 --> 00:22:04.989
Hey.

289
00:22:05.022 --> 00:22:07.125
Hey. That's my stuff. man.

290
00:22:07.158 --> 00:22:09.494
Hey. That's his bunk.

291
00:22:09.527 --> 00:22:11.563
You two a couple?

292
00:22:13.631 --> 00:22:16.668
It's OK...
I like the top better anyway.

293
00:22:18.836 --> 00:22:22.640
[man] Out of the 39.000 men
and women who make up
the United States Coast Guard.

294
00:22:22.673 --> 00:22:26.644
- There are only 280
rescue swimmers.
- Let's go! Let's go!

295
00:22:26.677 --> 00:22:28.780
This is because we are
the Coast Guard's elite.

296
00:22:29.046 --> 00:22:30.648
We are the best of the best.

297
00:22:30.681 --> 00:22:34.452
When storms shut down
entire ports. we go out.

298
00:22:34.485 --> 00:22:38.423
When hurricanes ground the
United States Navy. we go out.

299
00:22:38.456 --> 00:22:41.025
And when the Holy Lord Himself
reaches down from heaven

300
00:22:41.058 --> 00:22:44.796
and destroys His good work
with winds that rip houses
off the ground.

301
00:22:45.096 --> 00:22:47.699
we go out.

302
00:22:47.732 --> 00:22:51.669
And the attrition rate at this
school is well over 50 percent.

303
00:22:51.702 --> 00:22:57.108
So if by some miracle you
actually have what it takes
to become one of us.

304
00:22:57.141 --> 00:23:00.745
then. you get to live
a life of meager pay

305
00:23:00.778 --> 00:23:03.481
with the distinct
possibility of dying

306
00:23:03.514 --> 00:23:05.550
slow. cold and alone

307
00:23:05.583 --> 00:23:07.118
somewhere in the vast sea.

308
00:23:07.151 --> 00:23:12.590
However. you also get
the chance to save lives.

309
00:23:12.623 --> 00:23:16.461
And there is no greater calling
in the world than that.

310
00:23:16.494 --> 00:23:19.130
So. ladies and gentlemen.
welcome.

311
00:23:19.163 --> 00:23:23.101
Welcome to "A" School.
Are there any questions?

312
00:23:24.769 --> 00:23:28.773
Captain. Airman Fischer.
I just have one question.

313
00:23:28.806 --> 00:23:32.544
That guy who holds all them
records... Is he still alive?

314
00:23:32.577 --> 00:23:35.680
- Why do you ask?
- I just thought you ought
to let him know

315
00:23:35.713 --> 00:23:38.116
- I'm about to knock
his name off that board.
- Really?

316
00:23:38.149 --> 00:23:39.684
Why don't you let him know
yourself?

317
00:23:39.717 --> 00:23:43.721
He's standing right behind you
in the back of the room.

318
00:23:43.754 --> 00:23:47.826
Class. turn around and greet
Senior Chief Ben Randall.

319
00:23:48.125 --> 00:23:52.230
Senior Chief Randall
will be your lead instructor
for the next 18 weeks.

320
00:23:52.263 --> 00:23:56.501
Senior Chief Randall
is one of the most decorated
rescue swimmers

321
00:23:56.534 --> 00:23:59.671
in the history of the
United States Coast Guard.

322
00:24:01.205 --> 00:24:03.174
Ben. would you care
to address the class?

323
00:24:03.207 --> 00:24:06.244
No. I think there's been
enough talk for one day.

324
00:24:06.277 --> 00:24:09.514
Chief Skinner.
they're all yours.

325
00:24:09.547 --> 00:24:12.684
- Attention on deck!
- Carry on.

326
00:24:12.717 --> 00:24:14.686
Aye. captain.

327
00:24:14.719 --> 00:24:18.189
PT test begins at 0700 tomorrow.
Class dismissed.

328
00:24:18.222 --> 00:24:19.924
You will file through
the front door.

329
00:24:19.957 --> 00:24:21.793
First row first.
followed by the second.

330
00:24:21.826 --> 00:24:24.162
- Frank.
- [sighs]

331
00:24:24.195 --> 00:24:28.500
- When God rips houses
off the ground?
- [chuckling]

332
00:24:28.533 --> 00:24:30.268
I was rolling.

333
00:24:30.301 --> 00:24:32.537
And I didn't mean to put you
on the spot up there.

334
00:24:32.570 --> 00:24:33.938
[Skinner] Let's move. come on.

335
00:24:33.971 --> 00:24:36.241
I was real sorry
to hear about your crew.

336
00:24:37.575 --> 00:24:39.577
Come on. I'll show you around.

337
00:24:39.610 --> 00:24:42.847
So I hear you're staying
in a single?

338
00:24:42.880 --> 00:24:47.118
Yeah. Helen's got some
family business she's gotta
take care of up there.

339
00:24:50.221 --> 00:24:55.226
<i> [man] Mayday. mayday. mayday.</i>

340
00:24:55.259 --> 00:24:59.731
<i> We are on fire!
 We are on fire!</i>

341
00:25:14.211 --> 00:25:16.748
[gasping]

342
00:25:16.781 --> 00:25:20.752
[alarm beeping]

343
00:25:20.785 --> 00:25:23.254
- [whistle blowing outside]
- [man] Let's go!

344
00:25:23.287 --> 00:25:26.291
- Let's go. let's go. let's go.
- Get it. get it. get it.

345
00:25:26.324 --> 00:25:28.693
Let's move it now!
Let's move it out!

346
00:25:28.726 --> 00:25:30.728
Work as a team!
Work as a team!

347
00:25:30.761 --> 00:25:33.231
- [indistinct shouting]
- Hurry up!

348
00:25:33.264 --> 00:25:35.300
- Two lines.
- Two lines. Let's go.

349
00:25:35.333 --> 00:25:36.935
[chattering continues outside]

350
00:25:36.968 --> 00:25:39.637
[man shouting]
Where's my class leader?

351
00:25:39.670 --> 00:25:41.172
[sighs]

352
00:25:41.205 --> 00:25:45.744
[man shouting]
Turn around! Turn around.

353
00:25:47.812 --> 00:25:52.317
The only authorized command
to get you back up on your
feet is "pop tall."

354
00:25:52.350 --> 00:25:55.220
[all] Yes. Petty Officer Hall.

355
00:25:56.721 --> 00:25:59.223
- Do you understand me?
- [all] Yes. Petty Officer Hall.

356
00:25:59.256 --> 00:26:01.960
Very well. Let's try it.
Lean and rest.

357
00:26:03.861 --> 00:26:04.996
Pop tall!

358
00:26:06.297 --> 00:26:07.832
[out of synch] Ooh-rah.

359
00:26:07.865 --> 00:26:09.634
What the hell was that?

360
00:26:09.667 --> 00:26:12.303
That was terrible!
Let's try that again.

361
00:26:12.336 --> 00:26:15.807
Lean and rest! Together as one!

362
00:26:15.840 --> 00:26:17.776
[groaning]

363
00:26:19.377 --> 00:26:23.047
[grunting]

364
00:26:23.080 --> 00:26:25.783
- Twenty-two.
- Down. Up.

365
00:26:25.816 --> 00:26:27.652
- Twenty-three.
- Down. Up.

366
00:26:27.685 --> 00:26:29.988
- Twenty-four.
- Get that ass down!

367
00:26:30.021 --> 00:26:31.723
[all] Twenty-five.

368
00:26:31.756 --> 00:26:33.658
That is absolutely horrible.

369
00:26:33.691 --> 00:26:35.727
Pop tall. To the lone pine
and back.

370
00:26:35.760 --> 00:26:40.331
Go! Move your ass!
Let's move it! Get it going!

371
00:26:40.364 --> 00:26:43.935
[man] Let's go! Let's go!

372
00:26:43.968 --> 00:26:46.671
- Bring 'em back.
- [man] Circle back.

373
00:26:46.704 --> 00:26:50.642
- Let's go. Get back in line!
- Let's move!

374
00:26:50.675 --> 00:26:53.945
Right back in PT formation.
PT formation.

375
00:26:53.978 --> 00:26:55.380
PT formation.

376
00:26:55.413 --> 00:26:58.783
Lean and rest.
Senior Chief on deck.

377
00:27:03.387 --> 00:27:05.790
[straining]

378
00:27:05.823 --> 00:27:10.061
[marching cadence indistinct]

379
00:27:13.898 --> 00:27:16.834
[men chanting]
Don't need no land.
don't need no trees!

380
00:27:16.867 --> 00:27:20.372
[all straining]

381
00:27:26.944 --> 00:27:28.680
Mmm-hmm.

382
00:27:30.014 --> 00:27:33.418
- [straining continues]
- Pop tall.

383
00:27:33.451 --> 00:27:36.354
[all clapping] Ooh-rah!

384
00:27:36.387 --> 00:27:38.690
I don't care who you are.

385
00:27:38.723 --> 00:27:40.758
where you are from
or where you are going.

386
00:27:40.791 --> 00:27:42.460
I care about one thing
and one thing only.

387
00:27:42.493 --> 00:27:45.730
That is the future victims
you will be asked to save.

388
00:27:45.763 --> 00:27:47.732
If I feel that you
will fail them.

389
00:27:47.765 --> 00:27:49.100
I will fail you.
Understood?

390
00:27:49.366 --> 00:27:51.903
[all] Yes. Senior Chief!

391
00:27:53.938 --> 00:27:56.441
Hodge.
Where are you from. Hodge?

392
00:27:56.474 --> 00:27:59.077
I'm from T-Neck. New Jersey.
Senior Chief.

393
00:27:59.110 --> 00:28:01.913
Hodge is our triple repeat.

394
00:28:01.946 --> 00:28:04.415
Do you plan on making it
this time. three-peat?

395
00:28:04.448 --> 00:28:05.950
I really hope to. Senior Chief.

396
00:28:05.983 --> 00:28:07.351
Yeah.
well hope don't float. Hodge.

397
00:28:07.385 --> 00:28:10.788
You better start to learn
to swim against the current
and not with it.

398
00:28:10.821 --> 00:28:13.357
Aye. aye. Senior Chief.

399
00:28:13.390 --> 00:28:15.893
Fisch?

400
00:28:15.926 --> 00:28:18.830
Fisch. why are you here. Fisch?

401
00:28:18.863 --> 00:28:21.799
I'm here to exceed your
expectations. Senior Chief.

402
00:28:21.832 --> 00:28:25.770
I'm a rescue swimmer at heart.
Born. bred. and water-fed.
Ooh-rah!

403
00:28:25.803 --> 00:28:28.773
Wow. I'll bet you practiced
that all morning.

404
00:28:30.107 --> 00:28:32.343
Mr. Fischer is our
high school swim champ.

405
00:28:32.376 --> 00:28:35.079
He's had scholarships
to every Ivy League.

406
00:28:35.112 --> 00:28:38.950
Oh. I'm sorry. I didn't realize
that he was so qualified.

407
00:28:38.983 --> 00:28:41.920
I mean. you set records
in a pool?

408
00:28:43.120 --> 00:28:45.857
That's amazing.
I'll bet it was like. what.

409
00:28:45.890 --> 00:28:48.793
eight feet deep
in the deep end?

410
00:28:48.826 --> 00:28:50.995
What if your nose plug
didn't work?

411
00:28:51.028 --> 00:28:54.065
What if another swimmer
had cut into your lane.

412
00:28:54.098 --> 00:28:56.067
[stifling laughter]

413
00:28:57.501 --> 00:29:00.438
For the love of God.
you could have been killed.

414
00:29:02.139 --> 00:29:05.176
Your schedule says that
you will perform a PT test
this morning.

415
00:29:05.209 --> 00:29:07.044
That will not be necessary.

416
00:29:07.077 --> 00:29:09.814
Water is where you've been
called to serve...

417
00:29:09.847 --> 00:29:11.482
...water is where
you will be tested.

418
00:29:11.515 --> 00:29:13.885
[whistle blowing]

419
00:29:16.987 --> 00:29:19.524
This will serve in place
of your PT end test.

420
00:29:19.557 --> 00:29:23.528
This is a go/no-go exercise.

421
00:29:23.561 --> 00:29:26.130
You will tread water
for one hour.

422
00:29:26.163 --> 00:29:28.499
You touch the wall. you fail.

423
00:29:28.532 --> 00:29:33.871
You touch the bottom. you fail.
You fail. and you go home.

424
00:29:33.904 --> 00:29:36.808
Senior. this school operates
on a two-challenge rule.

425
00:29:36.841 --> 00:29:39.043
You can't throw them out
on their first day.

426
00:29:39.076 --> 00:29:43.014
If you cannot survive in a warm
pool of water. then you have no
business being here.

427
00:29:43.047 --> 00:29:44.582
Does this class understand?

428
00:29:44.615 --> 00:29:48.052
- [all] Yes. Senior Chief!
- Ooh-rah. class 5506.

429
00:29:48.085 --> 00:29:50.855
Now. who here can tell me
the rescue swimmer's motto?

430
00:29:50.888 --> 00:29:52.857
So others may live.
Senior Chief.

431
00:29:52.890 --> 00:29:54.892
Whoa. I feel safer already.

432
00:29:54.925 --> 00:29:58.429
You willing to sacrifice
your life so others may live.
Goldfish?

433
00:29:58.462 --> 00:29:59.997
Yes. I am. Senior Chief.

434
00:30:00.030 --> 00:30:02.967
You will have to earn
that right.

435
00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:06.137
I want all of you
to think about that.

436
00:30:06.170 --> 00:30:09.006
There is going to come a time

437
00:30:09.039 --> 00:30:11.542
when you reach
the point of exhaustion.

438
00:30:11.575 --> 00:30:13.277
You'll want to give up.

439
00:30:13.310 --> 00:30:17.949
The question is...
will you?

440
00:30:27.524 --> 00:30:30.228
[Skinner] There are three
letters that will set you free.

441
00:30:30.261 --> 00:30:34.232
D-O-R. Drop on request.

442
00:30:52.082 --> 00:30:55.887
Look at that.
A waste of time.

443
00:30:55.920 --> 00:30:58.890
[grunting]

444
00:31:04.094 --> 00:31:05.897
- You all right?
- Stay up.

445
00:31:05.930 --> 00:31:07.232
[gasping]

446
00:31:15.639 --> 00:31:17.208
[man] Somebody help him up!

447
00:31:19.176 --> 00:31:21.246
[indistinct shouting]

448
00:31:22.246 --> 00:31:23.981
[overlapping shouts]

449
00:31:24.014 --> 00:31:26.017
[man] Help him up.

450
00:31:28.686 --> 00:31:31.556
- Help him out.
- Hold him up.

451
00:31:38.162 --> 00:31:43.067
[overlapping shouts]

452
00:31:43.100 --> 00:31:45.670
Lyons. relax. man.

453
00:31:47.004 --> 00:31:49.007
[grunting. panting]

454
00:31:50.574 --> 00:31:53.010
You're dismissed.

455
00:31:53.043 --> 00:31:54.178
But. I cramped up.

456
00:31:54.211 --> 00:31:56.547
You're gone.

457
00:31:56.580 --> 00:32:00.018
[man] Let's go. Lyons.
out of the water.
Hurry up. let's go.

458
00:32:02.219 --> 00:32:03.554
On your feet.

459
00:32:05.022 --> 00:32:06.557
[Ben] First lesson
in physics. people.

460
00:32:06.590 --> 00:32:10.094
Muscle does not float.

461
00:32:11.695 --> 00:32:14.298
Petty officer Watson.
pull them out of the pool.

462
00:32:14.331 --> 00:32:17.134
Aye. aye. Senior Chief.
Let's go. people.
out of the water.

463
00:32:17.167 --> 00:32:21.372
[blows whistle] Hurry up!
Let's move people. hurry up!

464
00:32:21.405 --> 00:32:24.309
[man] Class winner. right here.

465
00:32:28.045 --> 00:32:31.950
I thought you said you
were willing to sacrifice
your life for another.

466
00:32:32.783 --> 00:32:34.685
I am. Senior Chief.

467
00:32:34.718 --> 00:32:37.755
Then why didn't you save
your teammate when he
reached out for you?

468
00:32:37.788 --> 00:32:40.658
[panting]

469
00:32:40.691 --> 00:32:43.194
I wasn't aware we were working
as a team. Senior Chief.

470
00:32:44.762 --> 00:32:47.031
That's the only way we work.
swim champ.

471
00:32:51.101 --> 00:32:53.604
Aye. aye. Senior Chief.

472
00:32:53.637 --> 00:32:55.306
[♪ Ozomatli:<i> Saturday Night]</i>

473
00:32:55.339 --> 00:32:58.175
<i> ♪ Get ready
 for the Saturday night ♪</i>

474
00:32:58.208 --> 00:33:01.112
<i> ♪ Dip. dive. socialize
 Get ready ♪</i>

475
00:33:01.145 --> 00:33:02.180
<i> ♪ Uh ♪</i>

476
00:33:03.347 --> 00:33:05.182
<i> ♪ Imagine waking up.
 solidarity is evident ♪</i>

477
00:33:05.215 --> 00:33:07.318
- Asshole.
- Come again.

478
00:33:07.351 --> 00:33:08.686
You heard me.

479
00:33:08.719 --> 00:33:11.122
Hey. Hey. Hey.
Ease up. Ease up.

480
00:33:11.155 --> 00:33:13.724
- What? Huh?
- It's not worth it.

481
00:33:13.757 --> 00:33:16.394
Good news.
I think there's an opening
on my buoy tender.

482
00:33:16.427 --> 00:33:18.363
I'll put in a word for you. huh?

483
00:33:20.831 --> 00:33:23.001
I'm really gonna
miss that guy.

484
00:33:29.206 --> 00:33:31.308
Hey. man.
what are you doing?

485
00:33:31.341 --> 00:33:33.344
You got your bunk back.

486
00:33:33.377 --> 00:33:37.715
<i> ♪ Hey. dip. dive ♪</i>

487
00:33:38.715 --> 00:33:41.085
- Captain.
- Ben. come in.

488
00:33:41.118 --> 00:33:43.220
You work fast.

489
00:33:43.253 --> 00:33:45.356
Lyons? He was one
of our top candidates.

490
00:33:47.124 --> 00:33:49.226
Sometimes you gotta
shoot a hostage.

491
00:33:49.259 --> 00:33:53.764
Look. we all know that
you're a legend. and all.

492
00:33:53.797 --> 00:33:56.367
but our program
has been proven to work.

493
00:33:56.400 --> 00:33:59.770
There's a gap between
training and what really
happens out there. Cujo.

494
00:33:59.803 --> 00:34:01.172
- Oh really?
- That's right.

495
00:34:01.205 --> 00:34:03.074
My intention is
to narrow that gap.

496
00:34:03.107 --> 00:34:06.210
If someone has a problem
with that idea.

497
00:34:06.243 --> 00:34:08.079
I'd like to hear about it.

498
00:34:12.516 --> 00:34:15.486
Is this how it's gonna be. sir?

499
00:34:18.222 --> 00:34:19.824
Yes. it is.

500
00:34:19.857 --> 00:34:22.393
Permission to be dismissed. sir?

501
00:34:22.426 --> 00:34:24.462
[Frank] Granted.

502
00:34:30.801 --> 00:34:33.437
Let's go. let's go.
Keep it together. Look tight.

503
00:34:33.469 --> 00:34:35.472
Keep it together.
Let's go. Let's move.

504
00:34:35.505 --> 00:34:39.342
You have three minutes to get
this gear on. All of it.

505
00:34:39.376 --> 00:34:40.811
[man] Set. go.

506
00:34:40.844 --> 00:34:44.215
[♪ Kasabian:<i> Club Foot]</i>

507
00:34:44.248 --> 00:34:46.384
Let's go!

508
00:34:49.887 --> 00:34:51.456
Are you ready?

509
00:34:53.590 --> 00:34:55.159
[whistle blows]

510
00:34:55.192 --> 00:34:57.128
<i> ♪ One... take control of me ♪</i>

511
00:34:57.161 --> 00:34:58.262
Hello. I'm a rescue swimmer!

512
00:34:59.329 --> 00:35:00.764
<i> ♪ Said it's two.
 it's another trick ♪</i>

513
00:35:00.797 --> 00:35:01.765
Don't quit on me.

514
00:35:01.798 --> 00:35:04.235
<i> ♪ Messing with my mind.
 I wake up ♪</i>

515
00:35:04.268 --> 00:35:06.303
<i> ♪ Chase down an empty street ♪</i>

516
00:35:06.336 --> 00:35:08.172
<i> ♪ Blindly snap
 the broken beats ♪</i>

517
00:35:08.205 --> 00:35:10.541
<i> ♪ Said it's gone
 with the dirty trick ♪</i>

518
00:35:10.574 --> 00:35:14.378
<i> ♪ It's taken
 all these days to find ya ♪</i>

519
00:35:14.411 --> 00:35:16.780
<i> ♪ Ah. ah. ah ♪</i>

520
00:35:16.813 --> 00:35:18.449
<i> ♪ I tell you I want you ♪</i>

521
00:35:18.482 --> 00:35:21.318
Do you hear me?
Do you hear me?

522
00:35:21.351 --> 00:35:25.322
Pop tall! Pop tall! Pop tall!

523
00:35:25.355 --> 00:35:27.558
[all yelling]

524
00:35:27.591 --> 00:35:30.427
If you make a mistake.
just fess up to it.

525
00:35:30.460 --> 00:35:32.563
take your licks.
and we'll press on.

526
00:35:32.596 --> 00:35:36.233
Everybody now is going to pay
for your potty mouth.

527
00:35:36.266 --> 00:35:40.471
- Down. Up... Down.
- [all] One!

528
00:35:40.504 --> 00:35:42.339
- Up.
- [all] Three!

529
00:35:42.372 --> 00:35:44.241
- Down. Up.
- [all] Five!

530
00:35:44.274 --> 00:35:47.344
[chanting]

531
00:35:47.377 --> 00:35:49.580
<i> ♪ Ah. ah. ah ♪</i>

532
00:35:49.613 --> 00:35:51.348
<i> ♪ I tell you I want you ♪</i>

533
00:35:51.381 --> 00:35:53.884
Are you crazy?
That's a command to get up!

534
00:35:53.917 --> 00:35:56.887
- [all] Ooh-rah!
- Get down. Get down.

535
00:35:56.920 --> 00:35:59.157
[cheering. yelling]

536
00:36:04.828 --> 00:36:07.331
<i> ♪ Ah. ah. ah ♪</i>

537
00:36:07.364 --> 00:36:09.533
<i> ♪ I'll say that I want you ♪</i>

538
00:36:09.566 --> 00:36:12.303
<i> ♪ Ah. ah. ah ♪</i>

539
00:36:12.336 --> 00:36:14.572
<i> ♪ I'll say that I need you ♪</i>

540
00:36:14.605 --> 00:36:16.574
<i> ♪ Ah. ah. ah ♪</i>

541
00:36:16.607 --> 00:36:19.243
[grunting]

542
00:36:19.276 --> 00:36:21.478
<i> ♪ Ah. ah. ah ♪</i>

543
00:36:21.511 --> 00:36:24.281
<i> ♪ Just wanted you near me ♪</i>

544
00:36:24.314 --> 00:36:27.185
- Ooh-rah!
- Ooh-r... [grunts]

545
00:36:38.395 --> 00:36:40.264
[air horn blows]

546
00:36:40.297 --> 00:36:42.967
<i> ♪ I say that I want you ♪</i>

547
00:36:44.301 --> 00:36:48.272
Ah. Can you die
from chlorine poisoning?

548
00:36:48.305 --> 00:36:51.408
I can't feel my legs.
I'm serious.

549
00:36:51.441 --> 00:36:53.944
Hoo... I don't know about
you guys. but I feel good.

550
00:36:53.977 --> 00:36:57.414
This Randall guy. he's operating
on some whole other cylinder.

551
00:36:57.447 --> 00:37:00.251
What is it. two weeks and he's
failed almost half the class?

552
00:37:00.284 --> 00:37:02.253
- Mmm-hmm.
- He's a legend.

553
00:37:02.286 --> 00:37:05.956
- They say he's got
something like 200 saves.
- I heard it was three.

554
00:37:05.989 --> 00:37:10.327
Who cares what his number is.
If he's such a stud. what's he
doing here?

555
00:37:10.360 --> 00:37:12.496
Whoo. How we feeling. boys?

556
00:37:12.529 --> 00:37:14.431
Hey. Z. where you going?

557
00:37:14.464 --> 00:37:16.433
My sister's best friend
is getting married

558
00:37:16.466 --> 00:37:19.270
and they're having
a big reception downtown.

559
00:37:19.303 --> 00:37:20.938
I promised her I'd go.

560
00:37:22.072 --> 00:37:25.409
You said a wedding reception?

561
00:37:25.442 --> 00:37:28.679
[yelling inside van]

562
00:37:28.712 --> 00:37:31.515
[chattering]

563
00:37:31.548 --> 00:37:33.017
All right. boys. let's go eat.

564
00:37:35.319 --> 00:37:40.557
<i> [woman] ♪ And if that
 mockingbird don't sing ♪</i>

565
00:37:40.590 --> 00:37:42.993
<i> ♪ Daddy's gonna buy you
 a diamond ring ♪</i>

566
00:37:43.026 --> 00:37:44.928
- Congratulations.
- Thanks.

567
00:37:44.961 --> 00:37:48.999
[chattering]

568
00:37:49.032 --> 00:37:54.038
[Ben] Yes. uh. Kodiak. Alaska.
The number for Helen Randall.

569
00:37:55.939 --> 00:38:00.344
Um... OK. try Helen Freeman.

570
00:38:02.779 --> 00:38:04.548
You betcha.

571
00:38:07.050 --> 00:38:10.087
[phone ringing]

572
00:38:10.120 --> 00:38:13.658
<i> [answering machine]
 Hi. You've reached Helen.
 Leave a message.</i>

573
00:38:13.957 --> 00:38:16.627
<i>Helen. it's Ben.
Jesus. that was weird.</i>

574
00:38:16.660 --> 00:38:20.564
<i>You haven't had to use your
maiden name since we were kids.</i>

575
00:38:20.597 --> 00:38:24.635
Helen. if you're there.
just pick up. We need to talk.

576
00:38:28.138 --> 00:38:30.041
<i>Please.</i>

577
00:38:36.046 --> 00:38:37.548
[turns off phone]

578
00:38:37.581 --> 00:38:41.452
[all laughing]

579
00:38:41.485 --> 00:38:45.656
All right. All right.
To those who have fallen.

580
00:38:45.689 --> 00:38:47.391
to those who have survived
phase one.

581
00:38:47.424 --> 00:38:49.526
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

582
00:38:49.559 --> 00:38:51.061
[overlapping chatter]

583
00:38:51.094 --> 00:38:54.598
And. and to our gal. Lindsey.

584
00:38:54.631 --> 00:38:57.668
You can rescue me anytime.

585
00:38:57.701 --> 00:39:00.104
- Oh. did he just say that?
- You did not just say that.

586
00:39:00.137 --> 00:39:02.706
- You did not just say that.
- You know what. Duran?

587
00:39:02.739 --> 00:39:05.576
You. I think I might
actually let drown.

588
00:39:05.609 --> 00:39:08.545
[all] Oh!

589
00:39:08.578 --> 00:39:12.416
<i> [woman]
 ♪ Don't you ever feel sad ♪</i>

590
00:39:12.449 --> 00:39:16.754
<i> ♪ Just lean on me
 when the times are bad ♪</i>

591
00:39:16.787 --> 00:39:20.557
Hey. Senior Chief.
Good to see you.

592
00:39:20.590 --> 00:39:21.792
Maggie is hot tonight.

593
00:39:22.993 --> 00:39:26.096
<i> ♪ In a bit of trouble
 and about to drown ♪</i>

594
00:39:26.129 --> 00:39:28.665
<i> ♪ Hold on. I'm comin' ♪</i>

595
00:39:28.698 --> 00:39:30.134
The place has not changed.

596
00:39:30.167 --> 00:39:35.072
<i> ♪ Hold on. I'm comin' ♪</i>

597
00:39:35.105 --> 00:39:37.708
- From Kodiak. Alaska...
- Don't.

598
00:39:37.741 --> 00:39:41.578
...Senior Chief Ben Randall
is in the house.

599
00:39:41.611 --> 00:39:43.781
Big as day and still alive.

600
00:39:43.814 --> 00:39:48.118
I must owe somebody money.
[laughing]

601
00:39:48.151 --> 00:39:51.188
- You're terrible.
- Oh.

602
00:39:51.221 --> 00:39:54.792
I heard a rumor you were gonna
be teaching here in town.

603
00:39:55.091 --> 00:39:58.562
If that ain't the karmic wheel
spinning. I don't know what is.

604
00:39:58.595 --> 00:40:01.465
[sighs] Well...

605
00:40:01.498 --> 00:40:03.567
To the prodigal's return.

606
00:40:03.600 --> 00:40:06.503
Where's your better half?

607
00:40:06.536 --> 00:40:08.806
She decided to stay home.

608
00:40:09.072 --> 00:40:11.708
- Oh. [laughing]
- Work stuff.

609
00:40:11.741 --> 00:40:15.879
Yeah. Winter in Kodiak.
Let me see.
winter in Louisiana.

610
00:40:15.912 --> 00:40:18.749
- Stop.
- And she decided to stay home.

611
00:40:18.782 --> 00:40:22.820
Well. it's a good thing we got a
full bottle and half the night.

612
00:40:22.853 --> 00:40:25.222
Yes. we do.

613
00:40:25.255 --> 00:40:26.657
[lounge music playing]

614
00:40:26.690 --> 00:40:30.727
Ooh. Check it out.
She's staring at you.

615
00:40:30.760 --> 00:40:33.864
- That girl right there
is not staring at me.
- Did you just point at her?

616
00:40:34.164 --> 00:40:36.733
- Did she see you point?
- I don't know.

617
00:40:36.766 --> 00:40:40.471
[chuckling] All right. now you
gotta go talk to her. You gotta
go make a move.

618
00:40:40.504 --> 00:40:42.673
- Yeah.
- I... I can't.

619
00:40:42.706 --> 00:40:45.175
I just don't feel comfortable
right now. talking to women.

620
00:40:45.208 --> 00:40:48.846
- You tell me you want to jump
out of helicopters for a living.
- You're talking to me.

621
00:40:48.879 --> 00:40:51.782
- but you can't talk to a girl?
- That's exactly what
I was telling you.

622
00:40:51.815 --> 00:40:54.751
All right. look.
I'm gonna help you out here.

623
00:40:54.784 --> 00:40:57.221
I'll show you how it's done.
[clears throat]

624
00:40:57.254 --> 00:41:00.891
Pick out the hottest girl
in here. I'll take her home.

625
00:41:00.924 --> 00:41:05.929
- Oh. gosh. Here he goes now.
- No. how about
I will find the girl.

626
00:41:05.962 --> 00:41:07.664
All right.

627
00:41:07.697 --> 00:41:09.834
- Okeydoke.
- Who you thinking?

628
00:41:10.133 --> 00:41:12.636
Make sure she's hot.

629
00:41:12.669 --> 00:41:16.640
- Where are you looking?
- OK. At the bar. uh...

630
00:41:16.673 --> 00:41:18.909
Two o'clock.

631
00:41:18.942 --> 00:41:23.547
- Oh. Yes.
- That's a good one.

632
00:41:23.580 --> 00:41:27.584
- That one?
- Yeah. that one.

633
00:41:27.617 --> 00:41:31.922
A hundred bucks says she shuts
you down in less than a minute.

634
00:41:31.955 --> 00:41:34.858
[chuckles] That looks
like a bet to me. Jake.

635
00:41:34.891 --> 00:41:36.126
That's a bet.

636
00:41:38.929 --> 00:41:40.197
All right.

637
00:41:40.231 --> 00:41:45.168
All right. A hundred bucks says
I close in less than a minute.

638
00:41:45.201 --> 00:41:47.671
Oh. Absolutely.

639
00:41:47.704 --> 00:41:51.575
- A little liquor.
- Hats off. man.

640
00:41:51.608 --> 00:41:55.579
- Tick-tock. tick-tock.
- The clock starts
when I talk to her.

641
00:41:55.612 --> 00:41:57.581
- That's fine.
- This is gonna be embarrassing.

642
00:41:57.614 --> 00:41:59.917
- All right. buddy.
- [man] What do you think?

643
00:41:59.950 --> 00:42:01.919
- Think he's gonna do it?
- [man 2] No.

644
00:42:05.922 --> 00:42:09.660
Evening. ma'am.
Can I buy you a drink?

645
00:42:12.329 --> 00:42:14.731
I don't think so.

646
00:42:14.764 --> 00:42:18.735
[whispering] You don't know
what you're missing.

647
00:42:18.768 --> 00:42:21.905
[scoffs]

648
00:42:21.938 --> 00:42:24.641
You sure you wanna go
with that one?

649
00:42:24.674 --> 00:42:27.211
That's like your top
of the line. A-game material?

650
00:42:29.913 --> 00:42:33.917
See. the way I see it.
you got two choices here.

651
00:42:33.950 --> 00:42:35.686
Walk away from me.

652
00:42:35.719 --> 00:42:38.322
or walk out of here
with me and split the cash.

653
00:42:39.923 --> 00:42:43.994
Cash? [scoffs]
What cash?

654
00:42:44.027 --> 00:42:47.331
The money you bet your friends
you could pick me up.

655
00:42:50.033 --> 00:42:53.771
- See. that makes me nervous.
- She's shutting him down.

656
00:42:55.972 --> 00:42:58.208
How much time you got left?

657
00:43:00.343 --> 00:43:03.847
- About 20 seconds.
- Shall we?

658
00:43:04.981 --> 00:43:07.618
- [Lindsey] Oh. my God.
- [Weatherly] No way.

659
00:43:07.651 --> 00:43:10.053
[Hodge] It looks like they're
leaving the bar together.

660
00:43:10.086 --> 00:43:13.323
No way.
You have got to be kidding me.

661
00:43:13.356 --> 00:43:15.292
- Unbelievable.
- How'd he do that?

662
00:43:15.325 --> 00:43:17.060
- I'm impressed.
- I'm impressed.

663
00:43:17.093 --> 00:43:20.330
There's a bar outside your base
called Maggie's. You know it?

664
00:43:20.363 --> 00:43:22.332
- Yeah.
- Good.

665
00:43:22.365 --> 00:43:24.935
Meet me there next Friday
around eight?

666
00:43:24.968 --> 00:43:29.607
- You got a name?
- Yeah. Don't forget my money.

667
00:43:33.376 --> 00:43:36.246
- [car starts]
- You got a middle name?

668
00:43:39.115 --> 00:43:42.653
You do realize I can't
go back in there?

669
00:43:42.686 --> 00:43:45.822
[alarm buzzing]

670
00:43:45.855 --> 00:43:47.691
This is the sound
of death knocking.

671
00:43:47.724 --> 00:43:50.728
SAR alarms and sleep
deprivation are part...

672
00:43:52.462 --> 00:43:55.032
Where the hell are they?

673
00:43:59.369 --> 00:44:03.641
[all shivering. shuddering]

674
00:44:06.843 --> 00:44:12.349
The first stages of hypothermia
are the most dreadful... Why?

675
00:44:12.382 --> 00:44:15.719
Because you still have
the ability to think. Say it.

676
00:44:15.752 --> 00:44:18.822
[all] We still have
the ability to think.

677
00:44:18.855 --> 00:44:21.425
The decisions you make
during this stage

678
00:44:21.458 --> 00:44:25.095
are gonna determine
whether you live or die.

679
00:44:25.128 --> 00:44:28.932
- [Ben] Is there a reason
you're not breathing. Goldfish?
- Huh?

680
00:44:28.965 --> 00:44:31.768
Is there a reason
why you're not breathing?

681
00:44:31.801 --> 00:44:36.006
I don't know anyone who can
stay alive without breathing
for 15 minutes. Senior Chief.

682
00:44:36.039 --> 00:44:39.042
Are you a coroner?

683
00:44:39.075 --> 00:44:42.479
Because pronouncing people
dead is not part of our job
description.

684
00:44:42.512 --> 00:44:46.349
- What do we always say?
- [all] There's dead.
and then there's dead.

685
00:44:46.382 --> 00:44:49.086
We never stop. Jake.

686
00:44:49.119 --> 00:44:52.355
Not from the cabin
to the tarmac. We never stop.

687
00:44:52.388 --> 00:44:54.891
- Aye. aye. Senior Chief.
- Understood?

688
00:44:54.924 --> 00:44:57.461
- [all] Yes. Senior Chief.
- OK. Jake. In the pool.

689
00:44:57.494 --> 00:45:00.397
- Hodge. you're up.
- You're with the dummy.

690
00:45:00.430 --> 00:45:02.799
[gasping]

691
00:45:02.832 --> 00:45:05.402
All right. now.
Three letters.

692
00:45:05.435 --> 00:45:08.906
Three letters will get you
people a cup of hot coffee
and a blanket.

693
00:45:10.540 --> 00:45:13.043
What do you say. Goldfish?

694
00:45:13.076 --> 00:45:15.979
I'm actually not that cold
anymore. Senior Chief.

695
00:45:16.012 --> 00:45:19.750
You're not cold anymore because
blood is moving from your...

696
00:45:19.783 --> 00:45:24.454
outer extremities to your heart.
That's why your arms won't work.

697
00:45:24.487 --> 00:45:27.924
You can plan on spending roughly
60 percent of your career

698
00:45:27.957 --> 00:45:30.894
in a mildly hypothermic state.

699
00:45:30.927 --> 00:45:33.363
Senior Chief. may I have a word?

700
00:45:47.076 --> 00:45:49.913
Yes. sir?

701
00:45:49.946 --> 00:45:52.949
Why wasn't I informed of this?
You know. we have classrooms.

702
00:45:52.982 --> 00:45:56.486
Your assignment is to simply
teach the stages of hypothermia.

703
00:45:56.519 --> 00:46:02.526
[shivering] Sir... In about
two and a half... minutes.
they'll understand.

704
00:46:06.129 --> 00:46:09.499
Permission to carry on. sir?

705
00:46:09.532 --> 00:46:10.968
Go ahead.

706
