01:01:20.509 --> 01:01:24.413
Come on. You're all fighting
for seconds. Just first loser.

936
01:01:24.446 --> 01:01:27.316
This is fun.
We'll pass out trophies later.

937
01:01:33.155 --> 01:01:34.790
Unbelievable.

938
01:01:34.823 --> 01:01:35.858
<i> ♪ Ain't no easy way ♪</i>

939
01:01:35.891 --> 01:01:38.761
<i> ♪ No there ain't
 no easy way out ♪</i>

940
01:01:38.794 --> 01:01:40.763
Unbelievable.

941
01:01:40.796 --> 01:01:43.365
<i> ♪ No there ain't
 no easy way out ♪</i>

942
01:01:43.398 --> 01:01:45.434
Want me to pull
these pansies out?

943
01:01:45.467 --> 01:01:49.939
<i> ♪ Ain't no easy way
 No there ain't
 no easy way out ♪</i>

944
01:01:52.875 --> 01:01:55.044
You do not want to hear
about my day.

945
01:01:55.077 --> 01:01:56.946
Yeah. I do.

946
01:01:56.979 --> 01:01:58.848
[groans]

947
01:01:58.881 --> 01:02:00.850
Man. this guy. Randall...

948
01:02:00.883 --> 01:02:05.488
You know. it doesn't matter what
I do. It's just not good enough.

949
01:02:05.521 --> 01:02:08.491
Well. maybe he's just trying
to push you to be better.

950
01:02:08.524 --> 01:02:10.926
You know. we teachers do that
to the ones we believe in.

951
01:02:10.959 --> 01:02:13.095
No. It's personal with me.

952
01:02:13.128 --> 01:02:15.131
He knows that I'm
better than he was.

953
01:02:15.430 --> 01:02:19.468
I mean. today I broke
every one of his records.

954
01:02:19.501 --> 01:02:21.170
I mean. it's like.
I own them all.

955
01:02:21.470 --> 01:02:23.038
Not all of them.

956
01:02:23.071 --> 01:02:25.508
There's one record
you won't break.

957
01:02:27.009 --> 01:02:29.512
<i>The Aegis.</i>

958
01:02:29.545 --> 01:02:32.948
Medical ship. caught on fire.

959
01:02:32.981 --> 01:02:35.384
It was a nightmare. People were
burning in their beds.

960
01:02:35.417 --> 01:02:39.388
And Ben Randall got every one
of those people off there.
except for this one guy...

961
01:02:39.421 --> 01:02:44.226
And right when the ship started
to go down. he reaches down
and grabs this guy...

962
01:02:44.259 --> 01:02:49.165
He's hanging from the cable
with this man's life in his
hands. and the winch jams.

963
01:02:49.198 --> 01:02:53.202
It's 20 minutes to the base.
The man's screaming...

964
01:02:53.235 --> 01:02:56.205
Ben looks him dead in the eye
and you know what he said?

965
01:02:56.238 --> 01:02:59.241
- He said "I won't let go."
- [Emily] What happened?

966
01:02:59.274 --> 01:03:02.211
Dislocated his shoulder.
tore every tendon in his hand.

967
01:03:02.511 --> 01:03:04.046
But. he didn't let go.

968
01:03:04.079 --> 01:03:07.850
Twenty minutes.
Just fingertips.

969
01:03:07.883 --> 01:03:11.020
You break that record.
then you give me a call.

970
01:03:25.567 --> 01:03:27.603
My day was all right.

971
01:03:27.636 --> 01:03:31.808
[♪ Abby Ahmad:<i> Tri-Me]</i>

972
01:03:43.118 --> 01:03:47.590
<i> ♪ I need to step outside ♪</i>

973
01:03:47.623 --> 01:03:50.860
<i> ♪ Another day
 marks another way marks ♪</i>

974
01:03:50.893 --> 01:03:53.128
<i> ♪ A new reason to hide ♪</i>

975
01:03:53.161 --> 01:03:57.299
<i> ♪ It's true when you slip
 you slide ♪</i>

976
01:03:57.332 --> 01:03:59.902
<i> ♪ On the ground
 I've been pushed down ♪</i>

977
01:03:59.935 --> 01:04:03.172
<i> ♪ By this primitive pride ♪</i>

978
01:04:03.205 --> 01:04:08.043
<i>♪ My voice a stifled symphony ♪</i>

979
01:04:08.076 --> 01:04:13.249
<i> ♪ My veins pump
 liquid lethargy ♪</i>

980
01:04:13.282 --> 01:04:15.618
<i> ♪ But I may be turning blue ♪</i>

981
01:04:15.651 --> 01:04:18.053
<i> ♪ And I may have
 some work to do ♪</i>

982
01:04:18.086 --> 01:04:20.923
<i> ♪ But try me ♪</i>

983
01:04:20.956 --> 01:04:24.994
<i> ♪ Tri-me ♪</i>

984
01:04:32.167 --> 01:04:35.538
[soft music playing]

985
01:04:39.007 --> 01:04:41.210
So here's my thinking:

986
01:04:41.243 --> 01:04:43.245
We should go on a date.

987
01:04:43.278 --> 01:04:46.081
[chuckles]
What do you call this?

988
01:04:46.114 --> 01:04:49.084
No. no. no. I'm talking
about like a real date.

989
01:04:49.117 --> 01:04:51.120
You know. with like
a nice restaurant.

990
01:04:51.153 --> 01:04:54.323
Some nice clothes.
I'll get you some flowers.

991
01:04:54.623 --> 01:04:56.992
I thought we agreed
to keep this casual.

992
01:04:57.025 --> 01:04:59.962
[stammering] Just one steak.
What is...?

993
01:04:59.995 --> 01:05:03.265
One steak is not gonna forge
some kind of a lasting

994
01:05:03.298 --> 01:05:06.135
emotional bond.

995
01:05:06.168 --> 01:05:08.137
I'm serious.

996
01:05:08.170 --> 01:05:11.040
- Yeah? So am I.
- Yeah.

997
01:05:11.073 --> 01:05:13.609
It's one dinner.
What's it gonna hurt?

998
01:05:13.642 --> 01:05:16.245
If you ordered a steak. I'd
imagine a cow would be involved.

999
01:05:16.278 --> 01:05:19.648
What. do you have an art gallery
over here? What is this 2?

1000
01:05:19.681 --> 01:05:24.119
Ah... It's so the guy behind me
knows what place he's coming in.

1001
01:05:24.152 --> 01:05:25.387
[laughs]

1002
01:05:25.420 --> 01:05:27.389
What about this one?

1003
01:05:27.422 --> 01:05:30.293
That... [grunts]

1004
01:05:30.592 --> 01:05:35.064
...is the initials of the guys
on my high school relay team.

1005
01:05:35.097 --> 01:05:37.232
A drunken celebration
gone wrong?

1006
01:05:37.265 --> 01:05:40.036
[mock laughing]
Something like that.

1007
01:05:41.436 --> 01:05:44.673
- So. about this date...
- Oh. God. Just dinner. right?

1008
01:05:44.706 --> 01:05:46.275
No flowers.

1009
01:05:46.308 --> 01:05:49.678
Where we will discuss nothing
emotional or important.

1010
01:05:49.711 --> 01:05:53.148
[sighs] I am fully prepared

1011
01:05:53.181 --> 01:05:58.087
to do an entire hour on nothing
but the Chicago Bears.

1012
01:05:58.120 --> 01:06:01.657
And we can have completely
meaningless sex immediately
afterwards.

1013
01:06:01.690 --> 01:06:02.825
[gasps]

1014
01:06:02.858 --> 01:06:05.761
You think I'm gonna sleep
with you on our first date?

1015
01:06:05.794 --> 01:06:08.664
[scoffs] Think again.

1016
01:06:08.697 --> 01:06:11.367
- [laughing]
- You just head-butted me.

1017
01:06:11.400 --> 01:06:14.370
- [Jake] I'm gonna teach you
the breast stroke.
- [Emily laughs]

1018
01:06:14.403 --> 01:06:16.405
- It's very complicated.
- [Emily moans]

1019
01:06:16.438 --> 01:06:19.742
- Different than the butterfly.
- [chuckling]

1020
01:06:21.810 --> 01:06:26.615
[exhales] I guess...
I can't sleep.

1021
01:06:28.784 --> 01:06:31.453
Well. of course you can't.

1022
01:06:31.486 --> 01:06:34.189
Your wife left you.
Your best friend died.

1023
01:06:34.222 --> 01:06:36.058
You sound like
a damn country song.

1024
01:06:36.091 --> 01:06:39.094
- [grunts]
- If you had a dog.
it'd be run over by now.

1025
01:06:39.127 --> 01:06:40.462
So did she send you papers?

1026
01:06:40.495 --> 01:06:43.666
- Yeah.
- Did you read 'em?

1027
01:06:45.767 --> 01:06:47.202
No. I did not.

1028
01:06:47.235 --> 01:06:49.638
Well. you think
you might ought to?

1029
01:06:56.711 --> 01:06:59.081
You know. there never
was anyone else. Mags.

1030
01:06:59.114 --> 01:07:01.050
Like hell. Ben.

1031
01:07:02.117 --> 01:07:04.119
You're a bigamist.

1032
01:07:04.152 --> 01:07:06.789
You've been married
to the Coast Guard all along.

1033
01:07:06.822 --> 01:07:08.457
Give me that shoulder.

1034
01:07:08.490 --> 01:07:12.094
- [groans]
- You probably swum it
out of socket.

1035
01:07:12.127 --> 01:07:16.265
trying to prove
you was still 19. Am I right?

1036
01:07:19.801 --> 01:07:22.104
When the heck did we get old?

1037
01:07:22.137 --> 01:07:24.306
Hell. I've always been old. Ben.

1038
01:07:24.339 --> 01:07:26.175
You know what. though?
I don't mind.

1039
01:07:26.208 --> 01:07:29.111
I mean. if my muscles ache
it's because I've used them.

1040
01:07:29.144 --> 01:07:31.213
It's hard for me to walk up
them steps now.

1041
01:07:31.246 --> 01:07:33.115
It's 'cause I walked up 'em
every night

1042
01:07:33.148 --> 01:07:35.451
to lay next to a man
who loved me.

1043
01:07:35.750 --> 01:07:37.353
I got a few wrinkles
here and there.

1044
01:07:38.654 --> 01:07:43.292
but I've laid under thousands
of skies with sunny days. Yeah.

1045
01:07:43.325 --> 01:07:45.828
I look and feel this way.

1046
01:07:45.861 --> 01:07:50.265
well. 'cause I drank and I
smoked. I lived and I loved

1047
01:07:50.298 --> 01:07:53.402
and danced. sang.
sweat and screwed my way through

1048
01:07:53.435 --> 01:07:57.272
[chuckling]
a pretty damn good life.
if you ask me.

1049
01:07:57.305 --> 01:07:59.308
Getting old ain't bad. man.

1050
01:07:59.341 --> 01:08:02.311
Gettin' old. that's earned.

1051
01:08:20.929 --> 01:08:23.866
[gasps]

1052
01:08:23.899 --> 01:08:26.869
[exhales]

1053
01:08:35.410 --> 01:08:38.180
There will come a time
when you might have to decide

1054
01:08:38.212 --> 01:08:40.882
who lives and dies out there.

1055
01:08:40.916 --> 01:08:42.584
It's a terrible responsibility.

1056
01:08:42.617 --> 01:08:46.322
but it is one you will have to
make as a rescue swimmer.

1057
01:08:48.957 --> 01:08:51.827
The bigger reality is...

1058
01:08:51.859 --> 01:08:55.797
It's also something
you're going to have to
live with as a human being.

1059
01:08:58.966 --> 01:09:03.238
There will come a time when you
are going to have to say "no."

1060
01:09:04.538 --> 01:09:09.343
The most important person
to keep alive is yourself.

1061
01:09:09.377 --> 01:09:13.248
You'll be facing crews
from five to 20.

1062
01:09:13.281 --> 01:09:17.953
all saying. "save me. save me."
They're looking for a miracle.

1063
01:09:17.986 --> 01:09:21.590
- How old are you. Hodge?
- Twenty-four.

1064
01:09:21.622 --> 01:09:25.426
At twenty-four years old. you
have to become that miracle.

1065
01:09:25.460 --> 01:09:29.365
You have to find a way
to be that miracle.

1066
01:09:32.466 --> 01:09:35.636
Looking right.
Looking center.
Looking left.

1067
01:09:35.670 --> 01:09:37.606
Ooh-rah!

1068
01:09:44.578 --> 01:09:46.614
It's OK. sir.

1069
01:09:46.648 --> 01:09:48.817
- I'm a rescue swimmer. I'm...
- [grunts]

1070
01:09:57.959 --> 01:10:00.429
- [gasping]
- Again!

1071
01:10:06.034 --> 01:10:11.207
[muffled grunting]

1072
01:10:19.881 --> 01:10:21.984
[gasping. panting]

1073
01:10:22.017 --> 01:10:24.019
All right. that's it.
Time out.

1074
01:10:24.052 --> 01:10:25.621
Panics every time. Senior.

1075
01:10:25.654 --> 01:10:27.256
Hodge. over here.

1076
01:10:31.559 --> 01:10:33.529
Hey.

1077
01:10:37.332 --> 01:10:39.434
The only difference
between you and the victim

1078
01:10:39.467 --> 01:10:41.670
is the attitude in which
you enter the water.

1079
01:10:41.703 --> 01:10:46.408
You've gotta figure out a way
to be calm in the face of chaos.
Do you understand?

1080
01:10:50.345 --> 01:10:52.981
That's your first challenge.
Charlie.

1081
01:10:53.014 --> 01:10:56.552
One more. and you're gone.

1082
01:10:58.620 --> 01:11:01.991
- Come out.
- Aye. aye. Senior Chief.

1083
01:11:06.928 --> 01:11:08.631
- What's up?
- Hey. Fisch.

1084
01:11:17.372 --> 01:11:19.508
You don't have to take
his shit. Hodge.

1085
01:11:20.642 --> 01:11:23.312
What do you know?
It's so easy for you. Fischer.

1086
01:11:23.345 --> 01:11:25.914
Is that right?

1087
01:11:26.748 --> 01:11:28.617
[Hodge] Yeah.

1088
01:11:28.650 --> 01:11:30.519
No. you don't get it.

1089
01:11:30.552 --> 01:11:33.989
You don't realize
that you're tougher
than I am.

1090
01:11:34.022 --> 01:11:35.424
And how's that?

1091
01:11:36.625 --> 01:11:37.459
Well. if I get kicked out
of here. I'm not coming back.

1092
01:11:37.492 --> 01:11:40.028
I'm definitely not
coming back twice.

1093
01:11:40.061 --> 01:11:44.066
- I mean. you got guts. man.
- Stupidity.

1094
01:11:44.099 --> 01:11:47.303
How long you
been here. man?

1095
01:11:48.670 --> 01:11:51.740
All together. uh. I don't know.
Ten weeks first time.

1096
01:11:51.773 --> 01:11:53.642
six weeks. two days
second time.

1097
01:11:53.675 --> 01:11:55.610
Six weeks this time.

1098
01:11:55.643 --> 01:11:58.747
So you've been here longer
than anybody that's graduated.

1099
01:11:58.780 --> 01:12:01.450
But you don't think
you can make it.

1100
01:12:04.085 --> 01:12:06.521
Lighten up on yourself. man.

1101
01:12:06.554 --> 01:12:08.657
Let's go.
Let's get a beer.

1102
01:12:08.690 --> 01:12:12.761
Hey. wait. don't you have a date
with your girl from the wedding?

1103
01:12:12.794 --> 01:12:15.630
Yeah. but it's not till nine.

1104
01:12:15.663 --> 01:12:18.500
We got time. Get dressed.

1105
01:12:20.568 --> 01:12:23.105
- Let's go.
- [exhales]

1106
01:12:23.138 --> 01:12:25.540
[♪ Stevie "Funkworm" Butler:<i>
 Shake Up The World]</i>

1107
01:12:25.573 --> 01:12:27.376
Wait. wait.
Where are we going?

1108
01:12:29.010 --> 01:12:33.014
Uh. Jake. that's a squid bar.
There's Navy guys everywhere.

1109
01:12:33.047 --> 01:12:34.816
I don't give a shit.
A beer's a beer.

1110
01:12:34.849 --> 01:12:37.719
When pulling through the water.
you'll pull yourself through.

1111
01:12:37.752 --> 01:12:42.124
- [Hodge] Uh-huh. I'll go fast.
- You wanna pull it.

1112
01:12:42.157 --> 01:12:47.662
<i> ♪ With a bulletproof screen
 on the hood of my truck ♪</i>

1113
01:12:47.695 --> 01:12:51.099
Hey. Charlie. you get those
finished reports before you
came off to get tanked up?

1114
01:12:51.132 --> 01:12:54.636
- Yes. sir. captain.
- I'll believe that
when I see it.

1115
01:12:54.669 --> 01:12:58.607
We go to "A" School.
which is the most difficult
school in the military.

1116
01:12:58.640 --> 01:13:01.443
The attrition rate's like...
what is it. fifty percent?

1117
01:13:01.476 --> 01:13:04.413
- Fifty percent.
- It's over fifty percent.

1118
01:13:04.446 --> 01:13:07.082
We're still here 'cause
we're the best of the best.

1119
01:13:07.115 --> 01:13:12.187
When storms shut down entire
ports. you know who goes out?

1120
01:13:12.220 --> 01:13:16.558
Uh. we do. When hurricanes
ground the US Navy.

1121
01:13:16.591 --> 01:13:18.794
these little guys over here.

1122
01:13:18.827 --> 01:13:21.463
guess who goes out.
That's right. we do.

1123
01:13:21.496 --> 01:13:23.732
Look. honey. you better
keep it down in here. OK?

1124
01:13:23.765 --> 01:13:25.768
OK. honey. She called me honey.

1125
01:13:27.802 --> 01:13:31.807
OK. honey. But when God Himself
reaches down from heaven...

1126
01:13:33.475 --> 01:13:35.644
- What does he do. Jake?
- Rips houses off
the foundation.

1127
01:13:35.677 --> 01:13:39.181
When God Himself rips houses
off the foundation. we go out.

1128
01:13:39.214 --> 01:13:43.552
'Cause we are rescue swimmers
and that is our job.
and that's what we do.

1129
01:13:43.585 --> 01:13:46.054
You might want to
recheck your compass.

1130
01:13:46.087 --> 01:13:48.791
This ain't no puddle pirate bar.

1131
01:13:55.763 --> 01:13:59.835
Um. no problem. Because. uh.
we were just leaving anyway.

1132
01:13:59.868 --> 01:14:02.871
Sit down. Hodge. Drink.
Finish your beer. Drink.

1133
01:14:03.171 --> 01:14:06.675
- Yeah. sit. Hodge.
- That's my beer. man.

1134
01:14:12.547 --> 01:14:14.082
Finished now?

1135
01:14:15.917 --> 01:14:18.086
Must be happy hour.

1136
01:14:18.119 --> 01:14:19.721
[grunts]

1137
01:14:19.754 --> 01:14:21.823
[yelling]

1138
01:14:21.856 --> 01:14:23.158
[laughing]

1139
01:14:24.826 --> 01:14:26.762
- Back off.
- [grunts]

1140
01:14:28.596 --> 01:14:31.266
Everyone in this place
is retired Navy.

1141
01:14:31.299 --> 01:14:34.870
Hey. Hey. when do I
get that phone call?

1142
01:14:34.903 --> 01:14:38.574
I know I get a phone call.
When do I get my phone call?

1143
01:14:39.307 --> 01:14:43.178
[piano music playing]

1144
01:14:43.211 --> 01:14:46.581
Ma'am. I'm sorry. but
if nobody comes in 20 minutes.

1145
01:14:46.614 --> 01:14:47.916
I need the table.

1146
01:14:47.949 --> 01:14:50.518
- OK. Yeah.
- I'm sorry.

1147
01:14:54.589 --> 01:14:57.592
She's never gonna
talk to me again.

1148
01:14:57.625 --> 01:14:59.794
You know they'll
kick us out for this. right?

1149
01:14:59.827 --> 01:15:01.730
Yep.

1150
01:15:04.933 --> 01:15:06.869
At least they can't say we quit.

1151
01:15:08.670 --> 01:15:11.172
I was never gonna make it.
anyway. Skinner's right.

1152
01:15:11.205 --> 01:15:13.141
I panic every time.

1153
01:15:14.609 --> 01:15:17.145
Screw Skinner.

1154
01:15:17.178 --> 01:15:20.682
- I'm Skinner. Break my hold.
- Hey. what are you doing. man?

1155
01:15:20.715 --> 01:15:23.318
- Come on. Fischer. get off me.
- Clock's ticking. Break it.

1156
01:15:23.351 --> 01:15:26.221
Fischer. you're hurting me. man.
Fischer. get off me. man.

1157
01:15:27.722 --> 01:15:30.292
Come on. Fischer.
you're hurting me.
Fischer. man. get off.

1158
01:15:30.325 --> 01:15:32.594
- Break the goddamn hold.
- Fischer. get off me!

1159
01:15:32.627 --> 01:15:35.597
- Break the goddamn hold. Hodge.
- Fischer. get off me!

1160
01:15:35.630 --> 01:15:37.899
- [grunts]
- I said get off me!

1161
01:15:37.932 --> 01:15:42.237
All right. Now it's just like
that when you're in the water.

1162
01:15:46.040 --> 01:15:49.644
Well. now.
we can come back.

1163
01:15:49.677 --> 01:15:52.847
Give you boys time for a smoke
and some pillow talk.

1164
01:15:52.880 --> 01:15:57.019
[guards laughing]

1165
01:16:00.922 --> 01:16:01.990
[Fischer] Can't kick us out.

1166
01:16:02.023 --> 01:16:04.793
[Skinner] It's called
disorderly conduct. Yes. we can.

1167
01:16:04.826 --> 01:16:07.696
- We didn't fail at nothing.
- Our profession
is about control.

1168
01:16:07.729 --> 01:16:10.699
You both failed miserably
in that department.
Hold it right there.

1169
01:16:10.732 --> 01:16:12.935
- [Skinner knocking] Senior?
- Yeah.

1170
01:16:15.703 --> 01:16:17.272
Their disenrollment records.

1171
01:16:19.741 --> 01:16:22.344
- Bar fight?
- Mmm-hmm.

1172
01:16:22.377 --> 01:16:25.981
- All right. bring 'em in.
- Senior. Square it!

1173
01:16:32.420 --> 01:16:35.958
It's all my fault. Senior Chief.
Hodge had nothing to do with it.

1174
01:16:37.859 --> 01:16:40.362
- Is that true. Hodge?
- It's true.

1175
01:16:43.297 --> 01:16:47.035
All right.
Fine. you're dismissed.

1176
01:16:47.068 --> 01:16:51.039
- Senior Chief. I was...
- I said that you are dismissed.

1177
01:16:51.339 --> 01:16:53.642
Let's go.

1178
01:17:00.348 --> 01:17:03.685
You're gonna kick me out
for defending the Coast Guard?

1179
01:17:03.718 --> 01:17:05.687
The Coast Guard's been
around for 200 years.

1180
01:17:05.720 --> 01:17:08.790
I doubt a couple of knuckleheads
like yourself are gonna
defend it.

1181
01:17:09.090 --> 01:17:10.859
Sit down.

1182
01:17:13.995 --> 01:17:18.066
I've been trying to peel
the layers back on you
for a while now and I...

1183
01:17:18.099 --> 01:17:20.735
...I just don't get it.

1184
01:17:20.768 --> 01:17:24.372
I mean. this kind of work seems
a little remedial for someone
like yourself. you know.

1185
01:17:24.405 --> 01:17:27.809
Big swim champ. offer to every
Ivy League. you give it all up

1186
01:17:27.842 --> 01:17:31.413
to be here with us.
Why?

1187
01:17:31.446 --> 01:17:34.349
I'm here to save lives.
Senior Chief.

1188
01:17:36.884 --> 01:17:38.019
[exhales]

1189
01:17:38.052 --> 01:17:40.989
I spoke with
your coach. Jake.

1190
01:17:42.724 --> 01:17:45.326
- You spoke with my coach?
- Yeah. I spoke with your coach.

1191
01:17:45.359 --> 01:17:48.430
Something in your file just
kept... kept hanging me up.

1192
01:17:48.463 --> 01:17:51.766
You. uh. win the state
championship your freshman
and sophomore year.

1193
01:17:51.799 --> 01:17:53.902
then you don't swim
the next two.

1194
01:17:55.036 --> 01:17:58.006
I'm just a public school guy.
so. uh...

1195
01:17:58.039 --> 01:18:02.110
Pardon me. but it didn't add up
until... now.

1196
01:18:08.483 --> 01:18:12.787
"Kirk Holloway.
100 meter medley winner.

1197
01:18:12.820 --> 01:18:15.090
thrown through
the passenger window.

1198
01:18:15.123 --> 01:18:17.793
Pronounced dead at the scene.

1199
01:18:18.960 --> 01:18:22.764
Abe Ikeman.
first team All-American.

1200
01:18:22.797 --> 01:18:24.700
Lungs crushed.

1201
01:18:26.801 --> 01:18:29.070
Carl Sandoval.

1202
01:18:29.103 --> 01:18:32.874
50 meter freestyle champ. made
it all the way to the hospital.

1203
01:18:33.941 --> 01:18:36.011
Died of internal bleeding."

1204
01:18:44.952 --> 01:18:48.022
I guess you just know
everything. then.

1205
01:18:48.055 --> 01:18:51.126
I know what it's like
to lose a team.

1206
01:18:52.393 --> 01:18:53.928
Yeah?

1207
01:18:53.961 --> 01:18:57.899
What about living in a small
town where everyone thinks
you killed their brother.

1208
01:18:57.932 --> 01:19:00.969
or their son. or their best
friend? You know about that?

1209
01:19:01.002 --> 01:19:05.774
The kind of small town
where everyone still waves
to everyone...

1210
01:19:05.807 --> 01:19:08.376
just not to you?

1211
01:19:10.478 --> 01:19:15.517
I read the report. Jake.
Your blood alcohol was zip.
that night.

1212
01:19:15.550 --> 01:19:20.155
I'm guessing there was a flip
for designated driver. You lost.

1213
01:19:20.454 --> 01:19:22.891
I guess that just
makes it all go away. huh?

1214
01:19:22.924 --> 01:19:24.859
No. it doesn't
make it all right.

1215
01:19:24.892 --> 01:19:26.494
It just makes it an accident.

1216
01:19:26.527 --> 01:19:30.031
At least that's how it reads.

1217
01:19:30.064 --> 01:19:34.569
You were 16 years old. Jake.
I'm not your priest.
but if I was. I think...

1218
01:19:34.602 --> 01:19:37.405
...I think maybe
you deserve a pass.

1219
01:19:40.908 --> 01:19:42.844
You're giving me a pass?

1220
01:19:42.877 --> 01:19:45.013
You... You just think
you know everything.

1221
01:19:45.046 --> 01:19:47.015
With your psychobabble
bullshit.

1222
01:19:47.048 --> 01:19:50.118
- Why am I here?
- Why are you here? Huh?

1223
01:19:50.151 --> 01:19:53.021
You're too old to be doing this.
You washed up here.

1224
01:19:53.054 --> 01:19:56.858
You don't want to be teaching
a bunch of kids at a pool.
Am I right?

1225
01:19:56.891 --> 01:20:00.261
I don't give a shit what you
read. or who you talked to.

1226
01:20:00.294 --> 01:20:02.164
You don't know about me.
You don't...

1227
01:20:02.463 --> 01:20:04.833
I have me under control.

1228
01:20:09.103 --> 01:20:11.173
I can see that.

1229
01:20:29.056 --> 01:20:33.528
The only difference
between you and me is...

1230
01:20:33.561 --> 01:20:37.165
...I don't wear the ones
I lost on my arm. Jake.

1231
01:20:45.172 --> 01:20:47.475
I know where you're at. Jake.

1232
01:20:48.509 --> 01:20:50.478
I'm there myself.

1233
01:20:52.313 --> 01:20:56.117
I ask myself every day
why I was the one that survived.

1234
01:21:01.188 --> 01:21:04.092
- And?
- And...

1235
01:21:06.260 --> 01:21:08.029
And if I can't
answer that for me.

1236
01:21:08.062 --> 01:21:11.633
I'm certainly not going to try
and answer it for you.

1237
01:21:16.137 --> 01:21:17.606
Have a seat.

1238
01:21:24.111 --> 01:21:28.216
I want you to start being
a member of this team.

1239
01:21:28.249 --> 01:21:31.319
The team you have now.

1240
01:21:31.352 --> 01:21:33.521
You have a gift. Jake.

1241
01:21:33.554 --> 01:21:36.624
You're the best swimmer
to come through this program.
Hands down. by far.

1242
01:21:36.657 --> 01:21:39.060
You've got a whole
record board to prove it.

1243
01:21:39.093 --> 01:21:41.963
But you know what I see
when I look at it?

1244
01:21:41.996 --> 01:21:45.133
I see someone fast enough
who's gonna get there first.

1245
01:21:46.667 --> 01:21:50.171
I see someone strong enough
who's gonna last.
I see someone...

1246
01:21:50.204 --> 01:21:54.042
...who can save a life
that maybe nobody else could.

1247
01:21:55.977 --> 01:21:59.147
You really want to honor
the initials on your arm?

1248
01:22:00.081 --> 01:22:02.284
Then honor your gift.

1249
01:22:05.152 --> 01:22:07.589
Save the ones you can. Jake.

1250
01:22:08.589 --> 01:22:13.295
The rest... we've gotta let go.

1251
01:22:22.436 --> 01:22:25.606
Does this mean you're
not gonna fail me?

1252
01:22:25.639 --> 01:22:30.045
For what?
Backing up a buddy in a bar?

1253
01:22:32.313 --> 01:22:35.216
Man. I got bigger problems
than you.

1254
01:22:38.085 --> 01:22:41.189
I don't know about you.
but I could use a fucking drink.

1255
01:22:46.460 --> 01:22:48.296
Oops.

1256
01:22:50.097 --> 01:22:54.135
We're gonna consider everything
tonight off record and off duty.

1257
01:22:58.105 --> 01:23:01.209
- That was an invite.
- Oh.

1258
01:23:05.212 --> 01:23:07.315
You gotta be kidding me.

1259
01:23:07.348 --> 01:23:09.417
What was it they called you?

1260
01:23:09.450 --> 01:23:12.720
Puddle pirates.
But it's not... I'm...

1261
01:23:12.753 --> 01:23:15.690
I'm way over it.
Senior Chief. This is...

1262
01:23:15.723 --> 01:23:17.359
That's like sticks and stones.

1263
01:23:17.658 --> 01:23:19.260
Well. we'll just have one beer.

1264
01:23:19.293 --> 01:23:24.065
[country music playing]

1265
01:23:25.433 --> 01:23:28.403
Great.
They're angrier and drunker.

1266
01:23:28.436 --> 01:23:32.374
- Perfect.
- Hi. Two beers.

1267
01:23:32.706 --> 01:23:36.411
- You gotta be kidding me.
- That's what I said.

1268
01:23:36.710 --> 01:23:39.047
Look. I don't want
any trouble. OK?

1269
01:23:41.449 --> 01:23:44.318
They really don't like us.
do they?

1270
01:23:44.351 --> 01:23:48.123
No. They think they're
better than us because
they're combat-oriented.

1271
01:23:50.191 --> 01:23:52.693
We're the Coast Guard. Jake.

1272
01:23:52.726 --> 01:23:55.697
Nobody really appreciates us
until they need us.

1273
01:23:58.132 --> 01:24:00.301
Is that him?

1274
01:24:07.208 --> 01:24:09.411
Yep.

1275
01:24:13.114 --> 01:24:16.418
Hey. let me ask you a question
before we start bleeding.

1276
01:24:18.452 --> 01:24:21.122
All those saves...

1277
01:24:21.155 --> 01:24:24.092
What's your real number?

1278
01:24:29.296 --> 01:24:32.400
Do you have a death wish
or are you just shit stupid?

1279
01:24:34.435 --> 01:24:36.871
I'm gonna go with stupid
this time.

1280
01:24:36.904 --> 01:24:39.140
- Hi.
- Hi.

1281
01:24:39.173 --> 01:24:41.209
Who's this. your old man?

1282
01:24:41.242 --> 01:24:44.179
[chuckling]

1283
01:24:46.847 --> 01:24:49.217
You know. I'm really glad
you're still here.

1284
01:24:49.250 --> 01:24:51.419
- Oh yeah?
- Yeah.

1285
01:24:51.452 --> 01:24:54.422
[grunting]

1286
01:24:58.859 --> 01:25:02.497
- Behind you.
- [Navy chief] Stand down!
I said stand down!

1287
01:25:08.903 --> 01:25:11.272
I think you'd better leave.

1288
01:25:14.375 --> 01:25:16.444
OK.

1289
01:25:18.179 --> 01:25:20.181
Come on. Jake.

1290
01:25:23.350 --> 01:25:25.920
[country music continues]

1291
01:25:25.953 --> 01:25:29.190
All right. sit down.
Have a beer.

1292
01:25:29.223 --> 01:25:32.560
- That went a lot better
than I thought.
- Yeah.

1293
01:25:32.593 --> 01:25:36.430
- What the hell was that?
- I don't know.

1294
01:25:36.463 --> 01:25:40.568
Hey. uh.
I want to. uh. apologize to you.

1295
01:25:40.601 --> 01:25:45.273
About what I said earlier.
about you being old
and washed up and that.

1296
01:25:47.441 --> 01:25:49.343
Is there...?

1297
01:25:49.376 --> 01:25:51.279
Is there anything
you'd like to say to me?

1298
01:25:51.312 --> 01:25:53.247
Like what?

1299
01:25:53.280 --> 01:25:56.484
I don't know.
I apologized to you.
I just thought that...

1300
01:25:56.517 --> 01:25:59.387
You know. there might be
something you've said or done

1301
01:25:59.420 --> 01:26:01.455
that you'd like
to apologize to me for.

1302
01:26:01.488 --> 01:26:02.924
Why?

1303
01:26:04.325 --> 01:26:06.427
'Cause that's how
it's done. I...

1304
01:26:06.460 --> 01:26:09.330
You suck at apologies.
You know that?

1305
01:26:09.363 --> 01:26:11.465
I mean. you're missing
the whole concept.

1306
01:26:11.498 --> 01:26:13.935
[phone ringing]

1307
01:26:22.009 --> 01:26:25.580
<i> -</i> Hello?<i>
 - [Jake] Hi. It's me.</i>

1308
01:26:25.613 --> 01:26:27.582
[exhales]

1309
01:26:27.615 --> 01:26:31.485
Are you OK? What happened?
I mean. I waited for two hours.

1310
01:26:31.518 --> 01:26:36.257
Yeah... No. I'm...
I'm really sorry. I...

1311
01:26:36.290 --> 01:26:40.895
- What happened?
-<i> Um. it's a really long story.</i>

1312
01:26:40.928 --> 01:26:44.365
Let me just... [sighs]

1313
01:26:44.398 --> 01:26:48.869
Let me put it this way.
It was the...

1314
01:26:48.902 --> 01:26:52.473
...best worst night of my life.

1315
01:26:52.506 --> 01:26:54.609
Well. I'm glad someone had fun.

1316
01:26:59.580 --> 01:27:03.017
Can I... see you tomorrow night?

1317
01:27:03.050 --> 01:27:05.486
I have parent-teacher
conferences tomorrow.

1318
01:27:05.519 --> 01:27:08.389
What about the next night?

1319
01:27:08.422 --> 01:27:10.958
I have parent-teacher
conferences all week.

1320
01:27:10.991 --> 01:27:15.596
- You blowing me off?
-<i> No. Jake.</i>

1321
01:27:15.629 --> 01:27:18.299
I wouldn't do that to somebody.

1322
01:27:20.000 --> 01:27:23.437
<i> I gotta get up
 in a couple hours. I gotta go.</i>

1323
01:27:23.470 --> 01:27:25.339
Yep.

1324
01:27:25.372 --> 01:27:28.943
<i> Goodbye. [dial tone]</i>

1325
01:27:36.617 --> 01:27:40.021
[Ben] All right. You know
what we preached on the ground.
Same thing.

1326
01:27:40.054 --> 01:27:41.656
We're gonna stay together.

1327
01:27:41.689 --> 01:27:45.993
No matter what happens out
there. you stay together.

1328
01:27:46.026 --> 01:27:48.896
Whatever decision you make.

1329
01:27:48.929 --> 01:27:50.932
you make as a team.

1330
01:27:54.034 --> 01:27:57.405
We train to freefall
at 15 to 20 feet.

1331
01:27:57.438 --> 01:28:01.442
You fall from 50 feet.
that's like hitting concrete.

1332
01:28:01.475 --> 01:28:05.413
You fall 80 to 100 feet...
You die.

1333
01:28:12.453 --> 01:28:15.623
Hey. where are they going?
They're supposed to come back
for us. right?

1334
01:28:15.656 --> 01:28:19.026
I don't know.
Hodge. you've been here before.
They're gonna come back. right?

1335
01:28:19.059 --> 01:28:20.995
But I never made it this far.

1336
01:28:21.028 --> 01:28:24.699
- You're kidding?
- Not to the final week.

1337
01:28:24.732 --> 01:28:27.001
They're not coming back.

1338
01:28:27.034 --> 01:28:31.005
- What do we do?
- All right. Listen up.

1339
01:28:31.038 --> 01:28:34.675
We stay together as a group.
Nobody falls behind.

1340
01:28:34.708 --> 01:28:37.378
We all stay together.
One guy goes back.

1341
01:28:37.411 --> 01:28:39.413
we get him back up to the front.
OK? We're a team.

1342
01:28:39.446 --> 01:28:42.016
- Ooh-rah!
- Ooh-rah!

1343
01:28:42.049 --> 01:28:44.552
[Jake] Let's do it. 5506.

1344
01:29:20.721 --> 01:29:23.124
Sir. it's OK. I'm with
the US Coast Guard.

1345
01:29:23.157 --> 01:29:27.795
[grunting]

1346
01:29:50.551 --> 01:29:51.719
[Skinner] Again!

1347
01:29:51.752 --> 01:29:53.421
[grunts]

1348
01:29:59.126 --> 01:30:02.129
I'm a Coast Guard rescue
swimmer. I'm here to help you.

1349
01:30:02.162 --> 01:30:06.467
[blows whistle] Time out.
Class. pop tall.

1350
01:30:06.500 --> 01:30:09.437
Hodge. get yourself
to the side of the pool.

1351
01:30:09.470 --> 01:30:11.773
Aye. aye. Senior Chief.

1352
01:30:14.174 --> 01:30:15.510
[all] Ooh-rah!

1353
01:30:24.918 --> 01:30:26.687
Easy. Chief.

1354
01:30:27.888 --> 01:30:30.425
Guess that was
a lucky punch.

1355
01:30:32.793 --> 01:30:35.196
Hodge!

1356
01:30:37.197 --> 01:30:39.500
- You all right. Chief?
- You stay right there.

1357
01:30:49.576 --> 01:30:52.113
Well done. Charlie.

1358
01:30:54.281 --> 01:30:56.684
Well done.

1359
01:30:57.918 --> 01:30:59.787
Ooh-rah. Chief Skinner.

1360
01:30:59.820 --> 01:31:03.691
Class 5506. ooh-rah. Hodge.
On three...

1361
01:31:03.724 --> 01:31:07.695
- One. two. three!
- [all] Ooh-rah. Hodge!

1362
01:31:09.196 --> 01:31:11.232
Good for you.

1363
01:31:17.704 --> 01:31:21.709
- Get their gear off.
- [all yelling]

1364
01:31:21.742 --> 01:31:24.512
Get it off! Move!

1365
01:31:24.545 --> 01:31:25.580
I can't believe...

1366
01:31:26.713 --> 01:31:29.750
[all yelling]

1367
01:31:29.783 --> 01:31:34.755
[overlapping shouts]

1368
01:31:34.788 --> 01:31:37.225
- Get it off!
- Yeah.

1369
01:31:39.226 --> 01:31:43.731
Class 5506. will you come
find me if I am lost?

1370
01:31:43.764 --> 01:31:46.901
[all] Yes. Senior Chief!

1371
01:31:46.934 --> 01:31:49.703
Will you come save me
if I am drowning?

1372
01:31:49.736 --> 01:31:52.173
[all] Yes. Senior Chief!

1373
01:31:56.610 --> 01:31:59.280
I believe you would.

1374
01:31:59.313 --> 01:32:02.617
I have high hopes
for this class.

1375
01:32:08.655 --> 01:32:11.259
I have high hopes for you.

1376
01:32:14.294 --> 01:32:17.264
Matthew Stokes.
Savannah. Georgia.

1377
01:32:17.297 --> 01:32:20.701
- Matthew. job well done.
- Ooh-rah. captain.

1378
01:32:20.734 --> 01:32:23.904
Kenneth Weatherly.
Clearwater. Florida.

1379
01:32:23.937 --> 01:32:26.206
Go out there
and do great things.

1380
01:32:26.239 --> 01:32:30.210
William Hodge.
Astoria. Oregon.

1381
01:32:30.243 --> 01:32:33.881
- Where's Senior Chief?
- He had a chance to go back
to Kodiak. and he took it.

1382
01:32:33.914 --> 01:32:37.318
He never had much of a bedside
manner. He's a water dog. Jake.

1383
01:32:37.351 --> 01:32:39.820
As it turns out.
not a half bad teacher.

1384
01:32:39.853 --> 01:32:41.722
Best of luck.

1385
01:32:41.755 --> 01:32:45.660
Jacob Fischer.
Kodiak. Alaska.

1386
01:32:47.761 --> 01:32:50.965
- Congratulations. Jake.
Make us proud up there.
- Aye. aye. captain.

1387
01:32:51.264 --> 01:32:55.202
Scott Reeves.
Sitka. Alaska.

1388
01:32:55.235 --> 01:32:58.305
Ladies and gentlemen.
your graduates.

1389
01:32:58.338 --> 01:33:01.943
- [man] Ooh-rah.
- [applause]

1390
01:33:05.345 --> 01:33:07.648
- Congratulations.
- Thanks a lot.

1391
01:33:08.849 --> 01:33:11.352
- Good job. Weatherly.
- Good job.

1392
01:33:24.998 --> 01:33:28.035
- Sorry.
- [laughs]

1393
01:33:31.438 --> 01:33:35.943
- Well. congratulations.
- Thank you.

1394
01:33:40.447 --> 01:33:42.950
- I...
- It's OK.

1395
01:33:42.983 --> 01:33:45.719
We both knew where
this was going. right?

1396
01:33:45.752 --> 01:33:47.755
Just casual.

1397
01:33:48.989 --> 01:33:50.992
Right.

1398
01:33:53.460 --> 01:33:56.764
You're getting what
you've always wanted.

1399
01:33:58.031 --> 01:34:00.668
And always wanting more.

1400
01:34:03.336 --> 01:34:05.773
Take care of yourself. Jake.

1401
01:34:09.142 --> 01:34:11.646
[sighs]

1402
01:34:20.053 --> 01:34:23.057
- I gotta go to work.
- Yeah.

1403
01:34:45.779 --> 01:34:48.349
[sighs]

1404
01:35:01.762 --> 01:35:04.999
[seagulls squawking]

1405
01:35:53.580 --> 01:35:56.884
[man] Ladies and gentlemen.
welcome to the rock.

1406
01:35:56.917 --> 01:36:00.120
I'm Captain William Hadley.
C.O. of Kodiak air station.

1407
01:36:00.153 --> 01:36:02.823
- Fischer.
- Yeah. right here.

1408
01:36:02.856 --> 01:36:05.092
- Mr. Michetry will
square you away.
- Welcome.

1409
01:36:05.125 --> 01:36:09.530
The rest of you step up here
with Mr. Christiansen.
He will process you in.

1410
01:36:24.845 --> 01:36:26.847
Oh. amazing.

1411
01:36:26.880 --> 01:36:30.184
Not only does he come back
in great shape. but he
still thinks he can cook.

1412
01:36:30.483 --> 01:36:32.886
- Hello. Jake. Welcome.
- How you doing?

1413
01:36:32.919 --> 01:36:35.455
- Good to see you again.
- You guys keep it
warm here. huh?

1414
01:36:35.488 --> 01:36:38.793
Glad to know you know
where a free meal is.

1415
01:36:41.027 --> 01:36:44.031
And the stand team
arrives here next Tuesday.

1416
01:36:44.064 --> 01:36:46.867
Patch things up with the wife?

1417
01:36:48.535 --> 01:36:51.038
You fix things up
with that young lady?

1418
01:36:52.939 --> 01:36:55.242
Well. you still have
a choice. you know.

1419
01:36:57.944 --> 01:37:02.149
Hey. there was a question
I wanted to ask you
back in school.

1420
01:37:02.182 --> 01:37:06.119
And I didn't. But. um...

1421
01:37:06.152 --> 01:37:09.156
When you can't save 'em all...

1422
01:37:09.956 --> 01:37:12.226
...how do you choose who lives?

1423
01:37:12.259 --> 01:37:16.030
It's probably different
for everybody. Jake.

1424
01:37:17.497 --> 01:37:21.001
Kind of simple for me.
though. I just...

1425
01:37:21.034 --> 01:37:22.903
I take the first one
I come to.

1426
01:37:22.936 --> 01:37:26.173
Or the weakest one
in the group and I swim as fast.

1427
01:37:26.206 --> 01:37:31.545
and as hard as I can.
for as long as I can.

1428
01:37:33.246 --> 01:37:35.916
And the sea takes the rest.

1429
01:37:40.520 --> 01:37:43.924
Think I'm ready?

1430
01:37:43.957 --> 01:37:47.995
I'm not your teacher anymore.
Jake. I'm just your fellow
swimmer.

1431
01:37:48.028 --> 01:37:51.031
That's not exactly the answer
I'm looking for. there.

1432
01:37:51.064 --> 01:37:55.169
If I did not think you were
ready. I would not put you
in the Bering Sea.

1433
01:38:01.574 --> 01:38:03.677
<i>[woman on radio] 6030.
this is Kodiak Ops.</i>

1434
01:38:03.710 --> 01:38:05.712
<i>We are diverting your
training mission.</i>

1435
01:38:05.746 --> 01:38:10.284
<i> We've two young kayakers swept
 into the cave one mile south
 of Saltery Cove. How copy?</i>

1436
01:38:10.317 --> 01:38:12.953
[co-pilot] 6030 copies.
We're diverting at this time.

1437
01:38:12.986 --> 01:38:14.988
[pilot] We've got
a real case now. OK. guys.

1438
01:38:15.021 --> 01:38:18.692
High tides coming in and we've
got six to eight foot rollers
coming from the north.

1439
01:38:18.725 --> 01:38:21.228
Senior. what do you think
about taking Fischer with you?

1440
01:38:21.261 --> 01:38:24.064
I want him with me.
All right. he's good to go.

1441
01:38:24.097 --> 01:38:27.067
I don't think it's gonna be
a problem sliding in there.

1442
01:38:27.100 --> 01:38:29.369
I think the problem's gonna be
coming back out.

1443
01:38:29.402 --> 01:38:32.573
That's why I got Jake with me.
Got my human speedboat.

1444
01:38:35.375 --> 01:38:38.312
<i> [pilot] Kodiak Ops.
 this is 6030.</i>

1445
01:38:38.345 --> 01:38:40.114
<i> We're on scene at this time.</i>

1446
01:38:41.348 --> 01:38:44.952
No sign of kayakers.
I'm taking her down.

1447
01:38:50.023 --> 01:38:52.125
Cabin door is open and locked.

1448
01:38:52.158 --> 01:38:55.262
<i>[pilot] Those are definitely
ten foot waves.</i>

1449
01:38:55.295 --> 01:38:58.165
Swimmer is coming
through the door.

1450
01:39:00.200 --> 01:39:03.670
Remember. all right.
You've got the whole flank
of the ocean.

1451
01:39:03.703 --> 01:39:05.639
Punch her through that opening.

1452
01:39:05.672 --> 01:39:09.343
You gotta read the hydraulics.
you gotta count the waves.

1453
01:39:09.642 --> 01:39:12.046
Then wait for the flush.

1454
01:39:13.079 --> 01:39:15.382
[man] Checking swimmer.

1455
01:39:15.415 --> 01:39:18.319
Sure as hell hope you paid
attention in class. Speedboat.

1456
01:39:41.207 --> 01:39:44.345
Swimmers in the water.
swimmers OK.

1457
01:39:49.716 --> 01:39:52.619
Swimmer two is making contact
with swimmer one.

1458
01:40:28.321 --> 01:40:31.324
- Hey! Over here.
- Here.

1459
01:40:31.357 --> 01:40:35.328
- Over here.
- Shout out. Three o'clock.

1460
01:40:35.361 --> 01:40:37.164
[man] We're right here.

1461
01:40:40.133 --> 01:40:42.302
We're rescue swimmers.
We're gonna get you out of here.

1462
01:40:42.335 --> 01:40:44.337
I can't believe you guys
actually got here.

1463
01:40:44.370 --> 01:40:45.806
Give me your hand.

1464
01:40:48.408 --> 01:40:51.111
- Just the two of you?
- Yeah. His arm's hurt real bad.

1465
01:40:51.144 --> 01:40:53.180
All right.

1466
01:40:53.213 --> 01:40:56.249
Swimmer one. I got. uh.
two survivors.

1467
01:40:56.282 --> 01:40:58.485
It's gonna be
a basket pick up here.

1468
01:40:58.785 --> 01:40:59.720
-<i> [pilot] Roger.</i>
- Broken here?

1469
01:40:59.753 --> 01:41:04.124
You take him first.
Get him in the basket.

1470
01:41:04.157 --> 01:41:06.426
I'll follow with the other one
right behind you.

1471
01:41:06.459 --> 01:41:07.527
- You got that?
- Yeah.

1472
01:41:07.560 --> 01:41:08.628
- You got it?
- Yeah. yeah.

1473
01:41:08.661 --> 01:41:11.331
All right. I'm gonna lower you
down in here. all right?

1474
01:41:11.364 --> 01:41:14.201
Relax. buddy. I got you.

1475
01:41:14.234 --> 01:41:17.304
- All right. You're with me.
- OK.

1476
01:41:17.337 --> 01:41:19.473
[groaning]

1477
01:41:26.846 --> 01:41:28.482
I don't swim so good.

1478
01:41:28.515 --> 01:41:31.485
- You don't swim so good?
- No. sir.

1479
01:41:31.518 --> 01:41:34.321
That's OK.
I swim pretty good.

1480
01:41:34.354 --> 01:41:35.856
All right. on your back.

1481
01:41:51.371 --> 01:41:55.876
- Wait. Aren't we
gonna take the boat?
- I'm the boat.

1482
01:41:55.909 --> 01:41:58.879
Wait. wait. wait.
I'm afraid. I'm not ready.

1483
01:41:58.912 --> 01:42:01.314
- Hey!
- Wait. I can't go
without the boat.

1484
01:42:01.347 --> 01:42:03.250
Settle down!

1485
01:42:21.568 --> 01:42:24.905
[man] Something's not right.
Swimmer one's going back
to the cave.

1486
01:42:56.402 --> 01:42:58.371
What happened?

1487
01:42:58.404 --> 01:43:00.807
He hit a log.

1488
01:43:00.840 --> 01:43:03.510
What? What do you...?

1489
01:43:09.282 --> 01:43:11.552
[grunting]

1490
01:43:11.851 --> 01:43:14.555
[groaning]

1491
01:43:17.423 --> 01:43:19.926
- He's gone. Jake.
- He's not!

1492
01:43:19.959 --> 01:43:22.462
[coughing]

1493
01:43:22.495 --> 01:43:25.432
He's just got a head laceration!

1494
01:43:29.602 --> 01:43:32.372
- Here we go.
- [groaning]

1495
01:43:34.307 --> 01:43:36.510
Let's go.

1496
01:43:37.577 --> 01:43:39.646
Let's go!

1497
01:43:41.614 --> 01:43:44.884
Senior Chief. Randall.

1498
01:43:44.917 --> 01:43:46.587
Lock it in.

1499
01:43:49.422 --> 01:43:52.659
Simple physics. We're just gonna
time the flush. all right?

1500
01:43:57.330 --> 01:44:01.001
All right...
You call it. swimmer. [spits]

1501
01:44:08.508 --> 01:44:10.477
[Jake] Now!

1502
01:44:19.919 --> 01:44:23.657
Hey. I know you're tired. OK?
I know you feel tired right now.

1503
01:44:23.690 --> 01:44:28.395
I need you to keep your eyes
open. OK? All right? All right?

1504
01:44:28.428 --> 01:44:31.464
Hey. I need you to keep talking
to him. Keep talking to him.

1505
01:44:31.497 --> 01:44:34.467
Senior. Senior!

1506
01:44:34.500 --> 01:44:37.003
Can you open these up for me?

1507
01:44:37.036 --> 01:44:40.006
One by one I want you
to hand them to me.

1508
01:44:40.039 --> 01:44:42.676
Reyes. he's fine.

1509
01:44:44.477 --> 01:44:47.648
- Right here. buddy.
Right here. OK?
- [man] OK.

1510
01:44:52.652 --> 01:44:55.422
[woman crying] Robert!

1511
01:44:55.455 --> 01:44:57.991
- I'm OK.
- He's got a compound fracture
of his right radius.

1512
01:44:58.024 --> 01:44:59.926
We tried to stabilize
that a little bit.

1513
01:44:59.959 --> 01:45:03.363
We put a collar on this one.
but it was more precautionary
than anything.

1514
01:45:03.396 --> 01:45:06.566
- Thank you.
- This one's possibly
concussive.

1515
01:45:06.599 --> 01:45:08.735
We've been checking their vitals
the whole way back.

1516
01:45:09.035 --> 01:45:12.406
Their both mildly hypothermic
but I think they'll come around.

1517
01:45:13.673 --> 01:45:15.942
- Bye.
- Thank you so much.

1518
01:45:18.611 --> 01:45:21.415
You're welcome.

1519
01:45:24.016 --> 01:45:26.519
It happens. Ben.

1520
01:45:26.552 --> 01:45:30.324
Not to me.
Not like that.

1521
01:45:32.425 --> 01:45:36.963
I want you to sign them
in front of me.

1522
01:45:36.996 --> 01:45:40.767
- Why don't you take some
time to think about it?
- No. It's. um...

1523
01:45:41.067 --> 01:45:46.039
It's over. Just... sign them.

1524
01:45:51.043 --> 01:45:53.113
Please.

1525
01:46:16.569 --> 01:46:19.572
It could have happened
to anyone.

1526
01:46:19.605 --> 01:46:21.508
Maybe.

1527
01:46:21.541 --> 01:46:25.445
But what if it happens again?
What then?

1528
01:46:25.478 --> 01:46:28.448
The kid got a couple stitches.
He's gonna be fine.

1529
01:46:28.481 --> 01:46:32.452
- You got him out of there.
- No. you did.

1530
01:46:32.485 --> 01:46:36.122
You were strong
out there today.

1531
01:46:36.155 --> 01:46:38.525
I was proud of you.

1532
01:46:40.693 --> 01:46:43.463
What are you gonna do?

1533
01:46:43.496 --> 01:46:46.767
A friend of mine
once suggested fishing.

1534
01:46:48.100 --> 01:46:50.103
Think I might take his advice.

1535
01:46:50.136 --> 01:46:53.740
- Fishing?
- Yeah.

1536
01:46:53.773 --> 01:46:56.543
Well. guys like us
don't go fishing.

1537
01:46:56.576 --> 01:46:59.646
[chuckles]
Where have I heard that before?

1538
01:47:07.186 --> 01:47:09.622
Senior...

1539
01:47:09.655 --> 01:47:13.560
Before you go.
I gotta know one thing.

1540
01:47:13.593 --> 01:47:16.563
What's your real number?

1541
01:47:21.200 --> 01:47:23.570
Twenty-two.

1542
01:47:25.671 --> 01:47:27.674
Twenty-two?

1543
01:47:28.908 --> 01:47:30.877
That's not bad...

1544
01:47:30.910 --> 01:47:33.179
It's not two hundred.
but it's not...

1545
01:47:33.212 --> 01:47:36.616
Twenty-two is the number
of people I lost. Jake.

1546
01:47:37.783 --> 01:47:40.620
Only number I kept track of.

1547
01:47:57.270 --> 01:48:00.474
Keeps the sea out of your mouth.

1548
01:48:17.790 --> 01:48:20.827
[dog barking]

1549
01:48:31.737 --> 01:48:33.740
[door opening]

1550
01:48:39.312 --> 01:48:42.282
- Hey.
- Hi.

1551
01:48:44.684 --> 01:48:47.554
You started painting again?

1552
01:48:47.587 --> 01:48:50.590
Yeah. Great light up there.

1553
01:48:50.623 --> 01:48:52.292
Yeah.

1554
01:48:57.763 --> 01:49:00.934
You know. um...

1555
01:49:00.967 --> 01:49:04.304
I want to apologize
for the phone calls. Helen.

1556
01:49:05.805 --> 01:49:09.309
I should have given you
your space.

1557
01:49:09.342 --> 01:49:13.580
And you felt showing up here
unannounced was the best way
to communicate that?

1558
01:49:19.852 --> 01:49:21.755
Hey.

1559
01:49:45.978 --> 01:49:47.814
- Please just... Now just...
- Ben.

1560
01:49:47.847 --> 01:49:50.016
I. I... I want you
to have it. along with...

1561
01:49:50.316 --> 01:49:54.354
Along with these.
I... I signed them.

1562
01:50:01.761 --> 01:50:03.763
Why now?

1563
01:50:10.936 --> 01:50:12.805
I had a...

1564
01:50:12.838 --> 01:50:15.008
I had a case a while back.
you know.

1565
01:50:15.274 --> 01:50:17.711
A couple was drowning.

1566
01:50:19.311 --> 01:50:21.781
By the time I got there.
the husband was...

1567
01:50:21.814 --> 01:50:24.717
dragging his wife under. just...

1568
01:50:24.750 --> 01:50:28.021
trying to stay afloat.

1569
01:50:28.054 --> 01:50:30.790
Pure survival instinct.

1570
01:50:33.325 --> 01:50:36.829
It took me. um...

1571
01:50:36.862 --> 01:50:41.067
It took me a long time
to understand that...

1572
01:50:41.100 --> 01:50:43.770
...that man was me.

1573
01:50:46.706 --> 01:50:49.409
- [exhales] Oh. man.
- [beeping]

1574
01:50:49.442 --> 01:50:51.811
Doggone it.

1575
01:50:51.844 --> 01:50:53.946
[turns off beeper]

1576
01:50:53.979 --> 01:50:56.082
Sorry.

1577
01:50:58.317 --> 01:51:00.086
Aren't you gonna
answer that?

1578
01:51:03.422 --> 01:51:06.092
I'm not a rescue swimmer
anymore. Helen.

1579
01:51:30.783 --> 01:51:32.985
[sniffling]

1580
01:51:33.018 --> 01:51:35.455
My baby.

1581
01:51:37.790 --> 01:51:41.895
[door opens and closes]

1582
01:52:01.881 --> 01:52:03.082
Lock it up!

1583
01:52:03.116 --> 01:52:08.020
We have a 75 foot fishing vessel
taking on water in high seas.

1584
01:52:08.053 --> 01:52:12.092
She's dead in the water
with four souls on board.

1585
01:52:12.391 --> 01:52:15.895
With its de-watering pumps
unable to keep up.

1586
01:52:15.928 --> 01:52:19.399
it's not a matter of if this
thing is going down. but when.

1587
01:52:32.244 --> 01:52:35.381
[man yelling indistinct]

1588
01:52:42.221 --> 01:52:45.391
[yelling indistinct]

1589
01:52:55.201 --> 01:52:58.504
- [alarm beeping]
- [radio chatter]

1590
01:52:58.537 --> 01:53:02.876
<i> [Ben] There will come a time.
 when you are going to have
 to say no.</i>

1591
01:53:04.109 --> 01:53:07.013
<i> You'll be facing crews
 from five to 20.</i>

1592
01:53:07.046 --> 01:53:10.583
<i>All saying. "save me. save me."</i>

1593
01:53:10.616 --> 01:53:14.086
<i> They're looking for a miracle.</i>

1594
01:53:14.119 --> 01:53:18.858
<i> At 24 years old.
 you have to find a way
 to be that miracle.</i>

1595
01:53:18.891 --> 01:53:21.828
[pilot] Sounds good. We'll
plan our freefall deployment
to the water.

1596
01:53:21.861 --> 01:53:23.496
- You good with that. Jake?
- Copy that.

1597
01:53:23.529 --> 01:53:26.999
OK. if we have to put you in.
we're gonna get you in upswell.

1598
01:53:27.032 --> 01:53:28.901
and let the waves take you
down to the boat.

1599
01:53:28.934 --> 01:53:30.903
- You good with that?
- Roger.

1600
01:53:30.936 --> 01:53:33.139
We're only gonna have about
20 minutes on scene.

1601
01:53:33.172 --> 01:53:35.007
- So we gotta be quick.
- Copy that.

1602
01:53:35.040 --> 01:53:37.577
[pilot] All right.
I got the vessel in sight.

1603
01:53:37.610 --> 01:53:39.913
Two o'clock. about 50 meters.

1604
01:53:45.150 --> 01:53:46.452
[yelling]

1605
01:53:46.485 --> 01:53:48.554
Cabin door open and locked.

1606
01:53:48.587 --> 01:53:52.191
Pre-rescue checklist
for freefall deployment.

1607
01:53:52.224 --> 01:53:55.862
Whoa. whoa! Boat just took
a wave. sir. One appears
to have gone on the edge.

1608
01:53:55.895 --> 01:53:58.097
- He's hanging from
the cargo net.
- [screaming]

1609
01:53:58.130 --> 01:54:01.033
- Get our swimmer down there.
- [radio chatter]

1610
01:54:01.066 --> 01:54:03.035
[man] Deploy up top.

1611
01:54:03.068 --> 01:54:06.939
Prepare for freefall deployment
of the rescue swimmer.

1612
01:54:06.972 --> 01:54:09.508
[screaming]

1613
01:54:09.541 --> 01:54:12.144
Rescue checklist part two.
Swimmer's getting ready.

1614
01:54:12.177 --> 01:54:14.647
Rescue checklist complete.
Swimmer's coming out.

1615
01:54:14.680 --> 01:54:16.282
[pilot] Roger that.
Check swimmer.

1616
01:54:16.548 --> 01:54:19.619
Swimmer's at the door. sir.
Checking swimmer.

1617
01:54:19.652 --> 01:54:22.088
Swimmer ready?

1618
01:54:22.121 --> 01:54:24.624
God help you if you ain't. boy.

1619
01:54:28.327 --> 01:54:31.164
Swimmer's away.

1620
01:54:38.537 --> 01:54:41.507
Swimmer's OK. He's heading
toward the vessel.

1621
01:54:47.980 --> 01:54:50.984
He's cutting through
those waves pretty good.

1622
01:55:11.637 --> 01:55:16.075
That's it. He's approaching the
vessel... He's at the boat. sir.

1623
01:55:22.381 --> 01:55:24.984
Man. are we glad to see you!

1624
01:55:27.052 --> 01:55:30.990
<i> [man on PA] Coast Guard
 Cutter</i> Alex Haley<i> ten miles
 southwest of Ashlock.</i>

1625
01:55:36.996 --> 01:55:41.667
<i> [pilot] Kodiak Ops. Rescue
 6034. Fischer is on board.
 but vessel is compromised.</i>

1626
01:55:41.700 --> 01:55:45.171
<i> Taking on lots of water.
May not hold much longer.
 Stand by for further...</i>

1627
01:55:45.204 --> 01:55:48.207
How many guys you got on here
and is anybody injured?

1628
01:55:48.240 --> 01:55:51.143
I've got four guys.
This guy's got a broken leg.

1629
01:55:51.176 --> 01:55:54.113
Skipper's down below.
He's trying to save the pumps.

1630
01:55:54.146 --> 01:55:57.149
All right. He's gonna go first.
All right!

1631
